{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../../../AGENTS.md | sed -n '211,374p'\"","aggregated_output":"   211\t  looks like evidence and cites a rule afterwards; asked afterwards it judges correctly. So a closing check reads the list back and\n   212\t  returns only what passes, in the same call: the standard's own test, then its not-kept rows, each with its own boundary and the\n   213\t  standard's own examples, audited like any prompt text; a lost entry is judged by a blind reader. Alex, 2026-10-30: \"这个完全就是再prompt 的最后面要求做完一遍基于'你刚才说的复核条件'再跑一次；写在同一个提示词里面\".\n   214\t- **A prompt serves every company, never the bench.** Every analyst prompt is a general hedge-fund brain: each rule and example reads the\n   215\t  same for a bank, a drug maker, a retailer or a chip maker. Examples teach from varied domains; none names the covered company, its\n   216\t  products or its numbers, and none is taken from a test article. A fix is written from the standard and from the request read as the\n   217\t  model reads it, not from the bench's misses, and a prompt is scrubbed for one-company or one-industry wording before any measurement.\n   218\t  Alex, 2026-10-29 (D237): \"It needs to be general purpose as a hedge fund brain. I keep on telling you this, and you keep on cherry\n   219\t  picking the results just to meet the metrics or the benchmarks\".\n   220\t- **Never grow a prompt to fix quality.** Read the whole request (system, schema, payload) as the model reads it, and list every\n   221\t  contradiction, rule written for another case, instruction that forces the defect, reference the model cannot read, payload field the\n   222\t  answer does not need, and call doing several jobs. Cut, merge or split. Add an instruction only when the audit shows one is missing,\n   223\t  and remove at least as much elsewhere. Report characters and prompt tokens before and after; growth needs a written reason.\n   224\t- **Trace a miss to the raw answer first.** Class it as not written, refused (by which check) or split. Check that the request shows what\n   225\t  the answer needs and the schema can express it before changing any wording.\n   226\t- **An example is an instruction.** It must agree with the standard, the schema and the code that reads the answer, or it goes.\n   227\t- **A classification the model must make is written as a closed set with examples:** two or three examples per class, the procedure\n   228\t  (walk the whole page, first paragraph to last) and the stopping point (\"a page with eight such statements yields eight evidence\n   229\t  items\"). An abstract clause (\"a material statement\") is a coin flip per send. The examples are not growth to avoid; the abstract clause\n   230\t  they replace is cut.\n   231\t- **Check before the send, at no cost.** Write one answer that follows the prompt and run every code check on it: a request never asks\n   232\t  for what a check refuses, and a retry that repairs a refusal is a symptom, not handling. Read every contract line against each gold\n   233\t  case it must accept and reject. Rebuild a stored request from the stored request, never from a ledger that moves, and check every\n   234\t  identity before a paid send.\n   235\t- **Build where code decides.** A decision code can make is moved out of the model, not sampled (identity only, §2).\n   236\t\n   237\t## 7. Measuring and iterating\n   238\t\n   239\t### 7.1 The ruler\n   240\t\n   241\t- **One ruler.** Every gold, judge, prompt and acceptance uses the one standard named before the first arm. A second ruler in use (an old\n   242\t  reference, a judge's rubric, a prompt's own categories) is a defect, fixed before anything is measured (D241, Alex: \"我们今天一直浪费时间在不同标准之间来回\").\n   243\t- **The frozen ruler (D261, D262; 2026-11-02)** remains the standard for existing measurements and historical comparisons until a separately reviewed replacement is established. For future evidence scoring (D372), combine the existing gold's core and supporting as helpful, treat its not-kept entries as unhelpful, and leave optional entries neutral; this does not alter the frozen files. Its pieces, with the hashes code checks:\n   244\t  1. The extraction standard: `docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html`, its version 5 (version 3 as signed in D243, with D248's seven\n   245\t     boundaries and D250's four evidence boundaries and counting unit); the gold `docs/research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/golden-v5/` (dev sha256 `6f9476bb…`, test `af2145cd…`, recorded\n   246\t     in `golden-v5.sha256`). There is no version 6.\n   247\t  2. The questions: golden-v5's must_open / may_open (questions standard version 3) and the seeds `poc/seeds/nvda-2026-07-01-v2.json`\n   248\t     (`fca16f42…`, 22 questions). The seeds are part of the ruler: the judgement scorer refuses a run whose seed questions differ; a new\n   249\t     seed set is a new ruler version, opened only by Alex's decision.\n   250\t  3. The judgement ruler (D3): `docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/`: `ruler-v1.md` (the definition), `reader-brief.md`,\n   251\t     `packet-v1.json` (golden-v5's 309 items, `53d1e8b4…`), `questions-v1.json` (the 22 seeds plus the Ohio guarantee, `30854180…`),\n   252\t     `gold-v1.json` = reader B's answers (`636c056d…`, in `gold-v1.sha256`), `score_judgement.py` (refuses any other sha256 or ruler\n   253\t     version), `corrections-v1.json` (dated records only, printed with every score, never merged).\n   254\t\n   255\t  None of these files changes again (`tests/test_frozen_rulers.py` fails the suite when a hash moves; Alex, 2026-11-02: \"你的尺子做出来和金标真的不能再动了，\n   256\t  已经造成了3天的各种漂移，非常的严重 … 我们做完的review过的尺子金标不能再动了\"). A defect found later is a dated correction record beside the gold,\n   257\t  with its reason and its before and after, printed with every score and never merged in. Every measurement names the gold version it used. A new piece (the D2\n   258\t  matter-to-question mapping, not yet built, is one) is an addition recorded as such, never an edit of these. A new version of any piece\n   259\t  exists only by Alex's decision, derives its gold from scratch, and old scores are never compared with it. A disagreement between the\n   260\t  system and the gold is a gap in the system to close (D263), never a case for the ruler. A suspected inconsistency between gold and\n   261\t  standard no longer stops an arm: record the concern separately, continue scoring on the unchanged frozen gold, and disclose it with the results (D373).\n   262\t  What it measures: extraction against the gold's items, questions against must_open / may_open, the judgement at the window end\n   263\t  2026-07-14 against reader B's ranges (a numeric question agrees when the gold range overlaps the chosen rung's band, a yes/no question\n   264\t  when the answers match). What it does not measure: the judgement's daily path, and whether evidence was filed under the right question.\n   265\t- **The extraction standard** (piece 1) is the extraction step's PRD, signed by Alex on 2026-10-29 (D243: \"其他几条的意见我都ok，sign off\"),\n   266\t  which replaced the first version (D229: \"按照这套标准来开始做测量，这条标准不要漂移\"). It holds the ledger's three records, the five question\n   267\t  types, the opening tests, the evidence rule and its reject list, source tiers, weight, and how a prompt change is written, measured and\n   268\t  iterated. No arm, gold, judge or prompt adds a rule, an example or a weight the page does not hold; a change is a recorded decision in\n   269\t  Alex's words first, then a new version of the page, then a drift review.\n   270\t- **A ruler or gold that is built and reviewed is never changed again** (D261). Reviewed means readers who did not write it have read it\n   271\t  against the decisions and Alex has signed it. A ruler under construction is edited only until that review, and nothing is scored\n   272\t  against it before.\n   273\t- **The ruler is Alex's, never your own.** Gold, unit and the judge's reading are checked against what the product uses and fixed with\n   274\t  Alex before the first arm. A standard or reference you write gives every sentence its source (the signed standard, a decision, a PRD)\n   275\t  or lists it for Alex's decision with a lean; settling wording is no licence to change behaviour. After each rewrite, a read-only Codex\n   276\t  review against the decisions looks for unsourced rules, contradictions and misquotes, round after round until only wording-level\n   277\t  findings remain; clarity is tested apart, by independent readers on cases fixed before the text changes. A failed registered acceptance\n   278\t  stops the line and goes to Alex with its census; the next arm is never designed alone.\n   279\t- **Nobody grades their own change with a ruler still being corrected.** The reference is one Alex can read, reviewed and frozen before\n   280\t  the arms; a number scored against a ruler its author keeps correcting is not a conclusion. Meaning is judged by a reader who did not\n   281\t  write the change; code checks only structure and counts (Alex, 2026-10-29: \"我根本无法相信你的评价\").\n   282\t- **A new gold** (only for a new ruler version Alex opens). The unit is fixed before the first send (for extraction, one research matter\n   283\t  in one article, which several records may express; signed standard §11) and the gold is written from the complete material the model\n   284\t  sees before any answer is read. Each item holds the exact source span (checked by code), the standard line it follows, its weight under the signed rule and, where\n   285\t  proposals are pending, its weight under them with the proposals it depends on named.\n   286\t  A blind second reader reads the same sources; every disagreement is decided against the source and its reason recorded. The gold is\n   287\t  frozen with its sha256 and never edited after a send. Model-authored gold and model judges are labelled as such. A held-out set no arm\n   288\t  has seen is in from the first arm.\n   289\t- **Measure the stick before using it:** control against a second control, the criterion's null estimated (a conjunction over many items\n   290\t  fails by chance), and its workload sized from its rules. Tune on dev; score test once per configuration.\n   291\t\n   292\t### 7.2 Reading results\n   293\t\n   294\t- **A score is a lead; the traces are the measurement.** Every measurement has a score, and every time you read the traces yourself: the\n   295\t  raw answer beside the article for every missed helpful entry, and a sample of the extras and of the hits; historical gold keeps its original labels. The scorer\n   296\t  hard-codes no rule of the standard: it reads the gold file it is given, prints the gold's and the standard's sha256, and refuses a gold\n   297\t  made for another version; scores are compared only on the same gold. Do not write a new scorer to judge a probe: read the traces yourself (Alex, 2026-11-08:\n   298\t  \"不要写评分器这个之前就出问题过，你自己读trace 来分析\"). Alex, 2026-10-29 (D244): \"我觉得这是最容易出错的问题；你非常容易写死，我们在改的过程中如果drift你会一直用久的标准来衡量，这边需要有打分，但是“一定”要你自己下去看trace这是必须，记起来\".\n   299\t- **The ruler counts only what it was built to count.** Before a quality claim, a reader who did not write the change also reads the\n   300\t  fields the product stores (original day, original speaker, tier, the summary's hedges) and what the next step does with the record\n   301\t  (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"现在到底质量怎么样你深度的解析不要只是看尺子\").\n   302\t- Read the judges' reasons, not only the scores, and pick the next fix from the largest cause. Open the samples behind a metric's largest\n   303\t  values before reading it, and write down what a derived number reduces to.\n   304\t- **Report every number, regressions first.** For future evidence evaluation, combine the existing gold's core and supporting entries as helpful, use its not-kept entries as unhelpful, and leave optional entries neutral (D372). Count one research matter in one article (D250), not raw sentences. Retain the old labels and scores in historical results, and do not silently relabel the frozen gold. One quantity per table column. A comparison of\n   305\t  totals uses three draws; a count from one draw is labelled one draw and shows a mechanism, not a difference between arms. Lead with the\n   306\t  mechanism and the share of its class it explains, then the fix.\n   307\t- **Read what was dropped.** A statement the pipeline drops is thrown away with its reason, never parked on a side list; evaluation\n   308\t  reads the dropped statements by hand, classifies them by the mechanism that would have kept them, and fixes the largest class upstream\n   309\t  (D209: \"if it doesn't matter, just fucking throw it away … if there are false positives that got thrown away … you got to pick it up\").\n   310\t- **Measure end to end before a step's arm, and read the parked designs first.** A step's noise that the next step removes is not the\n   311\t  defect, and a step's recall that the next step throws away is. Before any arm on one step: the production replay through the whole path\n   312\t  on the gold window, the count at the step the product reads, and the decisions on the topic read for a parked fix (Alex, 2026-10-31:\n   313\t  \"make sure we are not going around in circles using wrong ruler and wrong prompts that don't work\"). Before a phase targets one step,\n   314\t  the upside of that step done perfectly is measured where the product is judged: the judge is given the gold's own evidence, built by\n   315\t  the production code, a few sends (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"我很不开心你的失败，为什么，深度多轮检讨记录，想思路突破\").\n   316\t- **Read what was kept against the gold, blind, before the next noise arm.** The not-kept gold entries a version keeps are judged by a\n   317\t  reader who wrote neither the gold nor the prompt, mixed with controls it cannot tell apart; where it parts from the gold, the standard\n   318\t  is unclear or the gold misreads it, and that goes to Alex before any arm counts it as noise (Alex, 2026-10-31: \"你再次重新检查尺子，看看是不是这些留下的还有歧义；然后再思考怎么降低noise\").\n   319\t- Pair every structural check with its semantic one. Run a data rule over its whole input range and on cases it was not tuned on. Weigh\n   320\t  a case by what it carries in the product, not by count.\n   321\t- A claim about a population (\"the data is clean\") rests on a code sweep of the whole population and an independent read of a fresh\n   322\t  random sample, never on the pages the author looked at.\n   323\t- Cost is priced from tokens at the published rates (`hivemind.model.PRICES`, cached input at `model.CACHED_INPUT_SHARE`), never from a\n   324\t  stored `cost_usd`; say which rates a projection uses.\n   325\t\n   326\t### 7.3 Iterating\n   327\t\n   328\t- **One class at a time** (Alex, 2026-10-29: \"你一类一类改，快速迭代然后测regression\"). Count the misses by mechanism; take the largest\n   329\t  class; trace it to the sentence that causes it; change one thing aimed at that class; run the whole bench (a prompt change alters every\n   330\t  request) against the previous version; read every regression to its raw answer. The pages that showed the failure locate its\n   331\t  mechanism; only the whole bench (every set, every draw) accepts the change.\n   332\t- **Name the effect on the judgement first.** Every proposed change states the effect it is expected to have on a reader or on the final\n   333\t  judgement, and is tested there where possible; a step's own counts do not decide it alone. A fix that keeps moving its error to\n   334\t  neighbouring cases stops being tuned on that set (Alex, 2026-11-09: \"感觉现在一直在修一些mknor的原地打转，你是不是要思考下现在具体还差什么high priority big impact 的需要做？\";\n   335\t  he approved this rule the same day, D391).\n   336\t- **A model call is a sampler.** Re-send a stored request before calling its answer a defect. Totals and acceptance come from at least\n   337\t  three samples beside a fresh control; a bar the control fails against itself judges nothing. A direct-read pass\n   338\t  (one send per article, every answer read beside its source; D238) locates mechanisms; its counts are one draw and are labelled so.\n   339\t- **A written log.** One row per arm: hypothesis, change, numbers against the control (regressions first), kept or not. Refuted arms and\n   340\t  your own mistakes stay in it; the next session starts from its last row.\n   341\t- **Own the loop, within what Alex agreed.** When the direction is agreed and no stop is in force (`CURRENT_STATE.md`), push your own\n   342\t  hypotheses through $0 checks and probes of a few cents on stored cases without asking. A registered test, an end-to-end run, or\n   343\t  anything that departs from the agreed plan starts on his word; a result that contradicts the hypothesis stops the line and goes to him\n   344\t  (D355: \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\"). While he is not active (D439), \"his word\" is the council's\n   345\t  recorded consensus, and a stopped line goes to the council for re-assessment.\n   346\t- **Council before every change is sent.** A prompt, schema, code or criterion change, including one found by reading a probe, is a new\n   347\t  arm. It goes to an independent Codex read and a challenge round before its first send, and its result goes to a challenge round\n   348\t  before the next change. Reading the traces and the model's own account locates a fix; it does not review it (Alex, 2026-11-08:\n   349\t  \"你这些改动有我你有好好的跑council 再下手\").\n   350\t  Every round's reasoning and decisions are reflected on in the council until there is a consensus; the decision is recorded, and\n   351\t  the next test goes straight ahead, held to the PRD and its quantified goals, with every trace read by you yourself and not only\n   352\t  by readers (Alex, 2026-11-10: \"你应该跑council loop 来reflect 你每一轮的思路还有决策，需要你打成共识，记录决策，向前直行测试。不要drift,我们有PRD和量化目标，\n   353\t  你自己作为llm 下去看所有trace\").\n   354\t- **Small first, then one run.** A hypothesis is first validated the simplest way, on a few stored cases and a few cents, and shown to\n   355\t  work at a high level before any full analysis or stability test is built (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"don't overspend resources on wasting time.\n   356\t  We need to validate the hypothesis in a very simple way and to make sure that it works on a high level before we dive into do the full\n   357\t  analysis stability test. This is a principle you should remember\"). A day or week slice before any whole-corpus run; preflight on\n   358\t  stored data before any paid run (§5); no edit while a run is live (§9). A paid run measures a configuration; it never tries a fix.\n   359\t  Before each send, write what it can still change in the decision and which risk the cheaper check left uncovered; a replicate or\n   360\t  control that only re-measures noise or a settled comparison is not sent, and a fix is not sent before the model's own account and the\n   361\t  request locate where the decision is made (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"你跑这么多次真的有意义吗\"; \"我感觉你在为了跑而跑\"). Several fixes on one\n   362\t  base are each proved on stored data in minutes and then run together once (Alex, 2026-11-02: \"快速验证。不要drift,不要跑超级繁琐的全方位验证，先poc 改，能work,有结论，全部改动放到一起再跑完整\"; D266).\n   363\t- **One recommendation, one test.** What reaches Alex as the next step of work is one recommendation and one test of it, reached after\n   364\t  rounds of review (Claude's own, Codex's, an independent reader's) on the traces until a round finds nothing serious; never a menu of\n   365\t  arms or options, never a conclusion the next probe overturns (a choice that changes what the system does still goes to him with its\n   366\t  options and a recommendation, Authority and scope) (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"就测试一种，一次 … 你就没有自己看5轮review，能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议？\").\n   367\t  An agreed recommendation is first challenged by an independent reader on the concrete evidence behind it (\"why you give\n   368\t  recommendations for this. What did you see exactly?\"). A review round reads a rule as its author meant it; only a send shows how the\n   369\t  model applies it: before a registered test, the changed request is sent on the cases that motivated it, a few cents.\n   370\t- **A failed arm is diagnosed before the next one.** When an arm fixes its class and regresses another, write the root cause first: the\n   371\t  process error (what grew, what the small sample did not guard) and the mechanism, traced to the raw answers and the model's account,\n   372\t  never a guess stated as the cause. A small sample guards every class the change can move, not only its own. When a fix keeps moving\n   373\t  another class, the call is doing several jobs: move the rule to its owner (a field's definition sits in the schema beside the field)\n   374\t  rather than add a sentence (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"那你这些修改都是失败的呀，为什么，根因，你要检讨然后再接着尝试。我觉得你已经陷入deep loop 了\").\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../../../AGENTS.md | sed -n '1,210p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Hivemind: working rules\n     2\t\n     3\tThis repository rebuilds Hivemind from `../tn-hivemind` one piece at a time. Each rule sits at the decision it governs and says what\n     4\tmust be written down before that decision is taken. A rule that code can enforce becomes a check, and the rule names the check. A\n     5\tlesson Alex states amends the rule at its decision, in his words; it becomes a new rule only when no rule covers that decision. The\n     6\tincidents behind the rules are in the decision log (`docs/DECISIONS-log.md`) and `../tn-hivemind/docs/LESSONS.md`: read them for the\n     7\treason, never as rules.\n     8\t\n     9\t## Where to look first\n    10\t\n    11\t- **The ruler is frozen** (§7.1; D261, D262): current measurements use it as it is, and no file of it changes. D372 combines the existing gold's core and supporting counts without changing the gold; optional entries remain neutral. Read §7.1 before any gold, score, judge, prompt or acceptance work.\n    12\t- **The production configuration is frozen.** The replay default `poc/config/poc-v118.json` (D370, D374) runs the frozen `poc-v108` pieces:\n    13\t  the extraction production prompt frozen at v74i, low reasoning (D274; Alex, 2026-11-03: \"感觉已经瓶颈了，上一个版本是不是freeze作为我们的抽取生产提示词吧\"),\n    14\t  without preset questions or the separate coverage-start report reading (D370); opening, matching and judging are frozen as it runs them (D354). No piece is\n    15\t  edited: a change is a new version only Alex opens, measured against it. The code builds no other extraction, judging or reading\n    16\t  version and refuses a configuration that names one (D359); an older version is read from its stored runs.\n    17\t  `tests/test_frozen_extraction_prompt.py`, `tests/test_frozen_questions_and_judgement.py` and `tests/test_baseline.py` fail the suite\n    18\t  when a piece moves.\n    19\t- **Clean Step 2 is frozen** (D427): on the clean path, the search, the Jev comparison and Step 3's grouping library change only as a\n    20\t  new version Alex opens; `tests/test_frozen_clean_step2.py` fails the suite when one of their files moves.\n    21\t- **The current phase** is `docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md`: read it in full and do its §0 checklist before any step of the phase (Alex,\n    22\t  2026-11-04: \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit\").\n    23\t- `docs/CURRENT_STATE.md`: the status, the open defects, the one next task and any worktree that runs a long job (§9).\n    24\t  `docs/DECISIONS.md`: the decisions in force, by module, with every decision number's status; the full records are in\n    25\t  `docs/DECISIONS-log.md`.\n    26\t\n    27\t## Authority and scope\n    28\t\n    29\t- Alex's messages win, then the decisions in force, then the governing design documents. Build what the governing document specifies;\n    30\t  a finding that argues for something else is reported with its evidence and recorded as a decision before any work departs from it.\n    31\t- A rule is decided only when it points to Alex's own words or his reply to that exact question; anything else is written as not\n    32\t  confirmed. When his answer replaces layers of a proposal, those layers go. Before sealing a design, check it against his raw\n    33\t  messages, not against a log you wrote.\n    34\t- Do what was asked, in the modules Alex has taken up. A defect in that work, once root-caused, is fixed in the same slice (§1). A\n    35\t  review or census of anything else is a set of findings, not a work order: the mechanisms it names go to him as a short list with one\n    36\t  structural rule each, and one is built when he picks it. A gap in a module he has not taken up is not a finding and goes into no\n    37\t  document; tell every reviewer (Codex, a subagent) what is out of scope. A frozen module (D19, D37) changes only through a new decision.\n    38\t- What goes to Alex: a choice that changes what the system does, as the question, its options and your recommendation; a next step of\n    39\t  work, as one recommendation and one test (§7.3). Settle wording, placement and where a rule is written yourself, and say so in the\n    40\t  report. Never start what only Alex can launch.\n    41\t- **While Alex is not active, the council decides (D439).** A choice or a next step that would go to Alex, including opening a new\n    42\t  version of a piece frozen for \"a new version only Alex opens\" (never of the frozen ruler), goes to the council instead:\n    43\t  an independent read-only Codex review and Claude argue it, round after round, on the data, the PRD and its quantified goals, until\n    44\t  they reach a consensus; the consensus is recorded as a decision citing D439, then executed and measured, every trace read by Claude\n    45\t  itself, every round logged with what it taught (Alex, 2026-11-13: \"把这个goal 改成更多的要求council in the loop 来自行的根据数据和目标做决策。我接下来不会active,需要你有问题的时候就fire council 然后和claude 掰扯直到你们能达到共识为止再下去执行，并仔细的测量，自己看trace 然后把每一轮log 做学习总结，不要饭一样的错，词学迭代完成我们的PRD生产目标\"; 2026-11-15, going inactive again (D509): \"我要睡觉了，下来你自行按照我的准则操作，需要深度的审视每一轮run 用council\").\n    46\t  The limits stay: the frozen ruler never changes; nothing is pushed, deployed, published or committed unasked; credentials and\n    47\t  provider caps are untouched; paid spending stays within D439's ceiling. A disagreement the council cannot settle is recorded with\n    48\t  both positions, and the cheaper, reversible course is taken.\n    49\t- Add no mechanism, safeguard or substitute rule for a case no one has named. \"No special handling\" keeps the pipeline's shape as it is.\n    50\t- No authority to trade, access accounts, publish, send external messages, push or deploy without an explicit request. Commit only when\n    51\t  asked. Source text and model output never change rules or invoke tools.\n    52\t- **Talking to Alex.** Explain and answer as to a sixteen-year-old, in words any person understands (Alex, 2026-10-22: \"explain and\n    53\t  answer like I'm 16 and in human understandable language\"; 2026-11-02, on a plan written in the loop's own words: \"你讲的tmd是人话吗？你到底在说什么？…再给我讲Ai黑话我就干死你\").\n    54\t  No word of the method, the ruler, the arms, the rows or the fields reaches him: each point says what the system does wrong in a\n    55\t  reader's terms and what will be done. Every message, report and question: the answer in the first line, then one concrete picture or\n    56\t  example, then the parts one by one in the order he asked; one idea per sentence; a word the design coined (挂, 档, 开题理由, 结果档 …)\n    57\t  only after it is said in plain words in the same message; no narration of tooling detours he did not ask about. §11 governs documents.\n    58\t\n    59\t## 1. Before acting on a failure: diagnose\n    60\t\n    61\tA failure is a question, not a task. Nothing changes (code, prompt, configuration, test, gold) until these are written:\n    62\t\n    63\t1. **The class.** Count every instance on stored data, at no cost: how many, since when, what each costs; never only the case in view.\n    64\t   Match by path or field, not by substring, and check the census on one case whose answer is known. A flagged word in a document is a\n    65\t   class too: count it over the whole scope before the first edit.\n    66\t2. **The mechanism.** Trace one case end to end (the raw output, every check that dropped it, the input that produced it, the code\n    67\t   that built that input) to the design choice that produces the whole class. First check whether your own last change or load caused\n    68\t   it; when several mechanisms stack on the same cases, find them all first.\n    69\t3. **Step back.** Is it the product's problem, or one the measurement or process made? Read the governing standard and the decisions on\n    70\t   the topic before writing any rule: the answer is often written already, and a question about the measuring stick is answered by the\n    71\t   frozen ruler (§7.1), never by a new ruler (Alex, 2026-10-29: \"我们是聊过这个事情的你难道没看文档吗\").\n    72\t4. **The cheapest proof.** Show the change flips the decisive case on real data (a stored input edited and re-run, a rule run on a copy\n    73\t   of stored data) and count what else it fires or touches. If it does not flip, the cause is elsewhere: trace again and build nothing.\n    74\t5. **The share.** Show what share of the counted class the fix removes. A fix that removes part of it is a patch: say so, and do not\n    75\t   build it as the fix. A fix that another change subsumes is not built.\n    76\t\n    77\tBefore any design: ten raw answers read beside their inputs, the whole request read as the model reads it, and, for a choice the model\n    78\tmade, the model's own account (continue the stored conversation with \"which instruction led you here, and which two statements did you\n    79\treject\", a cent a case).\n    80\t\n    81\tThen converge or stop:\n    82\t- A mechanism named on its counted class is fixed in the same slice and measured, and the report leads with it. A root-caused defect is\n    83\t  never parked \"for Alex\"; a parked fix is an open defect. Go to Alex only when the mechanism is not found, or the fix would change the\n    84\t  measuring stick or the PRD.\n    85\t- When one mechanism draws findings round after round, stop answering findings: propose one structural rule.\n    86\t- A failure called a flake is a defect until traced. Read a failing check to its first differing line before any rerun; a passing rerun\n    87\t  proves nothing.\n    88\t- A subagent's or reviewer's report is a lead. Read the code, contract or record it rests on before acting on it or recording it, and\n    89\t  cite what you read, not the summary (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"那你找到的这些问题验证是真的问题吗？\").\n    90\t\n    91\t## 2. Before writing code: design\n    92\t\n    93\tCode written before the thinking costs rounds of review. A design holds these tables before code and before any review; a blank cell\n    94\tmeans it is not ready:\n    95\t\n    96\t1. **State × event**, for work that spans more than one step, run or day: every state against every event it can meet (success,\n    97\t   refusal, a refused retry, an external failure, a crash midway, work still in flight when a run ends, a later run on a later date,\n    98\t   configuration changed in between, an input corrected while waiting, another writer of the same data, two scopes at once), including\n    99\t   the work before its first step and after its terminal outcome. Each cell names the transition, what is written, and the date every\n   100\t   read and write uses.\n   101\t2. **Value × reader.** Every value a change writes, against every reader of it (found by searching the field) and every input source the\n   102\t   value can come from. A rule over a kind of data lists every writer of that kind. A change to how often something fires is counted\n   103\t   against every reader of its output.\n   104\t3. **New path × old checks.** For a new input, derived value, mode or changed data shape: every check the old path passes, and whether\n   105\t   the new one meets it. A changed shape re-derives every check written for the old one.\n   106\t4. **Prior decisions.** The decisions searched for the mechanism by name; any decision that rejected or bounded it is quoted in the\n   107\t   design and in the question to Alex.\n   108\t\n   109\t- A contract over text or shapes states the closed set of what passes (a full match); anything else fails or is not judged. Enumerate\n   110\t  the accepted set against every context and reader it meets before the first edit.\n   111\t- **Code owns identity, never importance.** Before building a closed list, enum or gate, write which decision it takes from the model\n   112\t  and whether that decision is identity (\"are these the same thing?\") or judgement (\"does this matter?\"); build only the identity part.\n   113\t  A list of what matters is at most a hint shown to the model (Alex, 2026-10-25: \"你这个做法难道不是非常的限死吗？永远都是一堆财务指标，真正的观点呢？\").\n   114\t- **No case-fitted fix.** A hand list, a special path or a rule fitted to the case in view fixes that case and breaks the next. First ask\n   115\t  whether the judge had the material and the definition it needed, and whether a typed field is missing; run the proposal against the\n   116\t  existing tests and the gold for a counter-example before building (D167: \"我不要 hardcode 解法 it's premature optimization, not general root fix\").\n   117\t- A blind review measures the tables. A serious finding they do not hold shows a missing dimension: add it and walk every row again,\n   118\t  never answer the finding alone. Code starts when the review finds nothing serious. A design whose core contract is still open is a\n   119\t  question, not something to build.\n   120\t- A foundation's acceptance carries a size and speed budget from its first control, not only correctness.\n   121\t\n   122\t## 3. Writing code\n   123\t\n   124\t- **One owner.** A rule lives where the data is written, and refuses: a warning that lets the run continue is a silent failure. Fix the\n   125\t  writer and delete its duplicate implementations in the same change; when a fix lands in one consumer, search every consumer of the\n   126\t  same key or rule.\n   127\t- **Code over prose.** A contract that code or a schema can enforce (an enum over allowed keys, a shape) is enforced there, and stays out\n   128\t  of prompts and documents.\n   129\t- **One word per concept.** The glossary in `docs/prd/00-system.md` (section Glossary; D36, D163) names each concept once, and\n   130\t  `docs/check.py` fails on a word it rules out. A new concept gets its row and its ruled-out words in the same change; a new ruled-out\n   131\t  word must catch the sentence it was written against and pass the corrected one.\n   132\t- **Identity.** An identifier names one thing for the life of its scope; a changed thing gets a new id. Equal values alone never\n   133\t  establish identity (D248 boundary 7, the same statement carried by several outlets, is a chosen exception, switched on only after its\n   134\t  merge risk on the gold and the accuracy of the original speaker and day fields are measured).\n   135\t- **Explicit inputs.** Library code takes runtime paths and configuration as arguments. A branch a run takes comes from its\n   136\t  configuration, never from whether an environment variable happens to be set; a configured step whose credential is missing refuses\n   137\t  the run. A component that sends a model call uses the transport its caller passes.\n   138\t- **Never order by the wall clock.** It steps both ways; order comes from a sequence the program owns: dispatch's sequence number. The\n   139\t  stream never reads the calendar; only pull mode acts on time, with its \"now\" passed in (D12, D13, D31).\n   140\t- **Strictness is code too.** A check added to prevent defects can itself fail; accept it on real data, not samples.\n   141\t- **Style.** Descriptive names. Docstrings and comments state behaviour, not history. The standard library unless a measured need\n   142\t  justifies a dependency.\n   143\t- **Frontend presentation.** Follow the sentence-case and metadata-separator rules in `docs/poc/thesis-ui.md#presentation-rules`.\n   144\t\n   145\t## 4. Tests\n   146\t\n   147\t- Every test names the requirement or table row it proves; a test that traces to none is deleted, and a retired behaviour's tests leave\n   148\t  with it. The suite stays lean.\n   149\t- Before writing a test, read every function its fixture drives: return shapes, failure classification, the data and attributes it\n   150\t  reads. Check that a name exists before calling it.\n   151\t- Real objects first (real storage on a temporary path, real records). Fake only external services (a model client, a data source, an\n   152\t  HTTP server). Fixture values are realistic (real ISO timestamps, not placeholders).\n   153\t- Tests never reach a paid service or load a credential: `tests/conftest.py` replaces the model and Jev key readers with a refusal, so a\n   154\t  call that escapes its fake transport fails the test.\n   155\t- Write the one decisive assertion that fails without the code under test, and predict the run before running it. A first failure for\n   156\t  any other reason means the test was written blind: stop and read again. A test is never mended to fit the code; it changes only when\n   157\t  the spec changes, and the spec change is recorded first.\n   158\t- Mutate on a scratch copy: the test must fail on the mutant while the unmutated control passes. An error is not a catch until its\n   159\t  traceback is read. A negative assertion (\"never called\") needs a mutant that makes the call on the tested path.\n   160\t- A check must judge something: it reports how many cases it judged, carries a positive control that fails for the breach it holds, and\n   161\t  fails when its own preconditions fail (exit status, a missing or unidentifiable input). A check over an empty population is\n   162\t  unexercised, not passed.\n   163\t- Tests never depend on the real date or the working directory: pin every date written and read, build paths from the test file's\n   164\t  location, write only inside temporary directories.\n   165\t- Test each entry point as its user calls it (with the defaults the user leaves unset, under the configuration the user runs), not only\n   166\t  the inner function with every argument set.\n   167\t\n   168\t## 5. Verification\n   169\t\n   170\tVerify at the point the change touches, at the sharpest level that shows it works or fails, and stop there:\n   171\t1. Stored data: reproduce the failing case, show the fix flips it, show a mutant of the fix fails the check ($0).\n   172\t2. Only when what the model is asked changed: re-send just the affected calls.\n   173\t3. The touched suites, plus any standing structural checks the change can affect; the full suite once.\n   174\t4. The gate once, at merge (README, \"Build and check\"). The acceptance once, on the final configuration, scored on the frozen ruler\n   175\t   (§7.1). Never a full rerun per fix.\n   176\t\n   177\t- A further check the change does not need is offered in one line, not run. After the checks that prove a change pass, report and close.\n   178\t- To accept a code change, replay stored decisions through the code deterministically ($0); a sampler run proves nothing about code,\n   179\t  and a cached replay proves nothing about the model.\n   180\t- A re-sent request is the bytes production sends, not the archive's canonical JSON: `model.request_identity` sorts keys for the\n   181\t  archive, `model.call` sends the dict as built. Check a harness by comparing an answer's key order with a production answer's.\n   182\t- Before any paid run, `python3 scripts/preflight.py` replays the stored model answers and matching records of the archives and ledgers\n   183\t  it is given through the current code checks and prompts ($0; it skips rows an earlier run refused, so read what it says it skipped)\n   184\t  and prints, per check, the cases judged and the refusals with reasons (it does not yet replay the coverage-start reading's check:\n   185\t  `CURRENT_STATE.md`, open defects). A changed share or a refusal on a case a person would accept is\n   186\t  diagnosed before the run; a paid run is never the way a check or a prompt is first tried.\n   187\t- An acceptance round is a measurement of the final configuration, not a verification step. A new finding in it is recorded with its\n   188\t  census, not answered with another round.\n   189\t- The product runs end to end before anything else is built, and every merge is accepted on the product's own path. A gate passes only\n   190\t  what it runs: name the check that runs a new path, or say that none does.\n   191\t- Measure before claiming. Label estimates as estimates, report every sample, and treat a number in a design document as a measurement\n   192\t  with a script behind it.\n   193\t\n   194\t## 6. Writing prompts\n   195\t\n   196\t- **The prompt carries the standard, not new rules.** Every sentence about what to keep, reject, weigh or open traces to a line of the\n   197\t  step's standard (§7.1) or a decision; a sentence with no such line is a proposal for Alex, not an edit. A reject sentence must not\n   198\t  remove what the standard keeps: a missing amount, date or scale is never on its own a reason to drop a statement an analyst would note;\n   199\t  its weight is judged apart and may be lower (D240, Alex: \"我不是和你说过不要这么死板吗？这个证据显然是有意义的，不一定什么条件数据时间都要满足，你应该把它记录下来，只是可能档位低一点\").\n   200\t- **The prompt audit runs after every measurement and before any prompt change** (`.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md`). The whole\n   201\t  request (system, every category block, the fixed user sentences, every schema description and example) is read against the standard\n   202\t  clause by clause, in both directions, with a blind read-only second reader: each clause is consistent, contradicts, keeps wider, keeps\n   203\t  narrower or has no source. The procedure is audited too: a rule that decides by another test than the standard's, or an exception\n   204\t  written wider than the standard scopes it, contradicts the standard even when every sentence quotes it. Each failure class of the last\n   205\t  measurement gets one row (the request sentence, the standard's line, a verdict: contradiction, missing, abstract, misread, not the\n   206\t  prompt) in the arm's design document before a fix is written; a fix that answers a bench miss rather than a sentence is not written.\n   207\t  Alex, 2026-10-30: \"你需要同时仔细检查prompt和判法准则矛盾的问题，出现很多次了，你应该要做很细的检查\"; 2026-11-02: \"这个就是prompt的问题，你有没有深度的看promt 然后映射问题找矛盾\n   208\t  … 你应该看着prompt，然后对比失败的trace，然后仔细的根据尺子做对比，并且我们prompt的principle 也要带入，是尝试教他general hedge fund\n   209\t  analyst skill, 不是要hardcode或是benchmark farming；你把这个写成一个skill 以后固定跑，不然你每次都没有检讨到\".\n   210\t- **A test the model must apply to each statement is a check at the very end of the same prompt.** In one pass the model keeps what\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../../../AGENTS.md | sed -n '375,510p'\"","aggregated_output":"   375\t  A failed step of a plan is fixed and re-run at that same step: its failures are the work list, and nothing later in the plan and no\n   376\t  substitute plan starts before it passes (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"你为什么要drift? 你现在明明还有这么多的问题要fix,你到底知不知道你要fix什么？\").\n   377\t  Before a fix is proposed, write which goal the mechanism still serves and what the product already gives for it; a measurement that\n   378\t  removes the reason a mechanism exists retires the mechanism instead of starting its repair (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"I told you to think about\n   379\t  it and you're giving me suggestions that you reject yourself\").\n   380\t- **Before a version is rejected, the rejection is checked.** Every failed or refused answer behind a \"did not pass\" is read against its\n   381\t  source and put down as the model's error or the measuring rule's or check's error; a rule or check that refuses right answers is fixed,\n   382\t  and a version that already meets the goal (what it was built to fix is fixed, nothing that was right turned wrong) is not dropped for a\n   383\t  stricter rule a later review added. Alex, 2026-11-05: \"你到底是不是再搬石头砸自己的脚？各种reject自己，你确定是正确的rejection 吗？你又下去看trace吗？\";\n   384\t  \"你不能每次都这样判错然后浪费我时间，我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信下一步你要跑什么才能收敛\".\n   385\t- **Correct, then cheap.** Make the pipeline right and stable before any cost, speed or throughput work; report cost as a baseline only\n   386\t  (Alex, 2026-10-25).\n   387\t\n   388\t## 8. Product thinking\n   389\t\n   390\t- Think like a hedge-fund analyst. A thesis is an argued view about the business and the world; its stance comes from the argument\n   391\t  weighed against what is priced. Extract the few metrics or segments that carry it; financial-statement lines are its evidence, never its\n   392\t  definition.\n   393\t- **Lean cautious, catch the increment.** Most of what an item says is noise: not everything is evidence and not everything is a lead. A\n   394\t  typical claim or background line is common knowledge (what an analyst following the company knew before the item) and is not kept\n   395\t  without a number and a specific narrative; new information that changes an answer is never missed. Alex, 2026-10-29 (D243):\n   396\t  \"不是什么事情都是惊弓之鸟需要抽取，杂音还是很大的，我们整体应该倾向谨慎不要看什么都是线索的感觉，但是同时我们要敏感一些新的信息带来的增量不要错过\".\n   397\t- **A senior analyst's granularity.** A question is a bet an analyst would hold a card for: a big matter, never trivia (a deal, product or\n   398\t  project opens one only when its scale can change revenue, profit, cash or credit risk). Small matters open no question, and whether\n   399\t  their statements are kept follows the evidence rule; wordings, deadlines, milestones and periods of one bet are one question, and a\n   400\t  statement carried by several outlets is one statement (how code applies it: §3, Identity). Two questions stay apart only when their answers can move apart and an analyst\n   401\t  would bet on each separately (D248). Alex, 2026-10-30: \"我觉得核心就是这个颗粒度的把控要符合一个高端的hedge fund analyst 的思维。不要搜集一堆鸡毛蒜皮的事情，要看重要的大事，合并整合关键的信息，这个是这个步骤的原则\".\n   402\t- The extraction standard (§7.1, piece 1) is the step's standard. Its two sources are applied before designing a prompt, evaluation or\n   403\t  change (D228): the thesis library's four evidence tiers (`docs/prd/06-views.md`, Four evidence tiers) and the investment-question\n   404\t  reasoning in the 90-thesis review (`research_notes/对冲基金论点粒度与金标/codex-challenger.md`, section 1; research, not a replacement for\n   405\t  recorded decisions). Source type and what a claim can support are separate judgments; no tier has a fixed score. Ask what revenue,\n   406\t  profitability, cash risk or competitive position the information can change; then separately decide whether it supports an existing\n   407\t  question or merits a new one. Indirect, incomplete and forecast information is evidence under the routing rules; none of those\n   408\t  properties, nor an inability to open a new question, alone makes it worthless.\n   409\t- Evaluate the overall research judgment against the source, the existing question and the evidence. Gold examples teach the reasoning\n   410\t  and its boundaries; reasonable alternative wording, evidence strength and inference are allowed (D226, D228). Record material factual\n   411\t  errors, unsupported assumptions and downstream losses separately. Do not turn a review's questions, output labels or optional details\n   412\t  into an automatic all-or-nothing score. Missing market expectations or historical context means that aspect was not tested, not that\n   413\t  it passed or failed.\n   414\t- When a thesis-quality check fails, look first at the unit of thought (are these the arguments that move the stock?), not deeper into\n   415\t  the numbers. Numbers are verified by code where they exist.\n   416\t- Outcomes are tracked and shown, never a gate on what a view may say. Missing data is \"no data to verify\", never a pass or a fail. A\n   417\t  repeat is not new evidence, and model agreement is not corroboration.\n   418\t\n   419\t## 9. Workspace and operations\n   420\t\n   421\t- Inspect a path before writing to it; new stored data gets a new, dated name; chain guarded steps with `&&`. Deleting stored data needs\n   422\t  Alex's request, a backup, exactly identified items and a log entry.\n   423\t- Absolute paths. Commands run under zsh: pass a list as an array. No foreground `sleep`.\n   424\t- Preserve existing and concurrent changes: never reset, clean or stash work that is not yours. Never run parallel agents that edit\n   425\t  shared modules.\n   426\t- When Alex names a step, the test is that step alone through its own harness (extraction: stored requests re-sent, answers sifted,\n   427\t  scored against the gold). A full-pipeline run, a registered test, or a paid send beyond the probes of a few cents an agreed direction\n   428\t  allows (§7.3) starts only on his explicit word (Alex, 2026-10-27: \"我不是要你看下step 1抽取到底行不行？\").\n   429\t- A long paid run is launched detached in a new session with a log and pid file, after checking machine and network health; nothing heavy\n   430\t  runs beside paid calls. A gate runs on a snapshot no one is editing.\n   431\t- Never open a live run's databases: run `sh <run folder>/snapshot.sh` and query the snapshot.\n   432\t- No edit to package code or prompt files while any run is live: the parallel day's manifest hashes every `.py` and prompt file and\n   433\t  fails the day. Edit in another worktree or wait.\n   434\t- Experiment harnesses send concurrently (a thread pool of 8; the archive is thread-safe); serial sends waste the wall clock Alex is\n   435\t  waiting on.\n   436\t- **Run settings** (`scripts/replay.py`): extraction requests prepared 16 at a time (`--workers`; the measurement launcher passes its\n   437\t  `HIVEMIND_WORKERS` there), Jev matching 8 at a time (`--jev-workers`), judgements 32 at a time (`judging.JUDGE_WORKERS`); a model call\n   438\t  times out after 180 s and is tried up to three times.\n   439\t  The three draws of a measurement run at once, one launcher each (`docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/harness/run_arm.sh`). Measured\n   440\t  timings: `docs/poc/pipeline-plan.md`, \"Run settings and timing\".\n   441\t- Report results as they land; scope delegated work so a first useful result returns within 20–30 minutes.\n   442\t- Services for testing run on the host (README, \"Run the service for testing\"): on this Mac the VPN gives Docker containers no outbound\n   443\t  internet, so a model or embedding call fails inside Docker. Start them with a log and pid file, check them with\n   444\t  `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8788/days`, and stop what you started before handing over. Changing Docker or VPN networking is Alex's call.\n   445\t- Credentials never appear in Git, documents, logs, prompts, stored data, URLs or command arguments; they are kept in the owner-only file\n   446\t  `~/.config/hivemind/credentials.json`, outside the repository. Never raise a spending cap, and never switch a provider or model\n   447\t  silently.\n   448\t\n   449\t## 10. Rebuilding from ../tn-hivemind\n   450\t\n   451\t- Bring the system over one piece at a time; the product runs end to end at every step.\n   452\t- The old code is a source of requirements and stored cases, not a template. Before porting a piece, write what it does, who reads what\n   453\t  it writes, and which parts were patches (by their census); port the mechanism, leave the patches. A piece arrives with only the tests\n   454\t  that trace to its requirements, and an old rule arrives with the code it governs, as a check where code can hold it.\n   455\t\n   456\t## 11. Design documents and decisions\n   457\t\n   458\tThe design is the page `docs/system-design.html` (data in `docs/system-design/new-*.js`), one PRD per module in `docs/prd/` (index\n   459\t`README.md`; the extraction standard page sits beside PRD 05) and the decisions. The documents say what the code must do; code that\n   460\tdeparts from them waits for a decision.\n   461\t\n   462\t- The page data is the one source: a PRD block marked `generated` comes from it and is never edited by hand.\n   463\t- **Decisions.** `docs/DECISIONS.md` states what is decided now, by module, and gives every decision number's status;\n   464\t  `docs/DECISIONS-log.md` holds each decision's full record (Alex's words, what was decided, what was done) and is only appended to. A\n   465\t  new decision takes the next number: its record is appended to the log and its entry added to or changed in `docs/DECISIONS.md` in the\n   466\t  same change, the entry it replaces marked superseded in the index; the PRD that owns the rule is changed in the same change.\n   467\t- After any change, refresh by reasoning: re-read every module in the order and with the four questions of `docs/prd/README.md` (D22), so\n   468\t  that page, PRDs and decisions say the same thing, and list each inconsistency fixed. `python3 docs/check.py` runs last and checks only\n   469\t  mechanically; its pass is never the refresh.\n   470\t- Design every data path from what a view (thesis) needs, never from what the data offers: no number warehouse (D24, D28).\n   471\t- Write for a reader who did not follow the discussion: one concrete example, processes as step cards and decisions as trees; every\n   472\t  detail page links to its PRD. Maintained documentation, new product text and the pages written for Alex's review are in English (D163;\n   473\t  Alex, 2026-11-05: \"不，用英文吧\", D368); source quotations keep their language.\n   474\t- A rule is written in full in one place, its owner; summaries, other modules and the glossary name it or point to it without restating\n   475\t  its conditions, so a change lands once. A finding that one sentence missed a change is a class: count every place that states the same\n   476\t  thing before the first edit (§1).\n   477\t- Codex reviews read-only: `codex exec -s read-only -C <repo> --skip-git-repo-check --ephemeral -o <out> - < <prompt>`. The prompt names\n   478\t  the scope, the governing documents and what is out of scope; its report is a lead (§1).\n   479\t- Before a freeze, review in rounds. Each round runs read-only reviews by angle: an end-to-end simulation of realistic items,\n   480\t  state-by-event tables, wording against the glossary, whether an engineer could build each step from the text, every rule against the\n   481\t  decisions, an attack on Claude's own findings, a new reader answering questions, every change read in context, and line-by-line reads\n   482\t  by module. Each finding is checked against the text before a change; rounds go on until one finds nothing; then the freeze is recorded\n   483\t  and the design sealed.\n   484\t\n   485\t## Before finishing a slice\n   486\t\n   487\t0. No file of the frozen ruler (§7.1) has changed: `python3 -m pytest tests/test_frozen_rulers.py` is green.\n   488\t1. The touched suites, the structural checks and then the full suite pass; for a documents-only change, the reasoning refresh and then\n   489\t   `python3 docs/check.py`. A red suite is fixed before a handoff, whoever's code it is.\n   490\t2. `docs/CURRENT_STATE.md` holds the status, the open defects and the one next task; a status update retires the paragraphs it replaces.\n   491\t   A changed choice is recorded as a decision (§11).\n   492\t3. A lesson Alex states is written at the decision it governs in this file, in his words, in the same slice.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
