{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba paid_rehearsal.py; cat rehearsal.log'","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"$0 rehearsal of the judging-v13 paid gate: the provider stubbed at urllib.request.urlopen beneath the real budget transport, the real\n     2\tmodel.openai_transport and the real stop gate. Every HTTP body must equal, byte for byte, a request built here independently from the\n     3\tplan. Usage: python3 paid_rehearsal.py <scratch folder>   (runs every scenario; prints one line per check; exit 1 on any failure).\"\"\"\n     4\timport io\n     5\timport json\n     6\timport os\n     7\timport sys\n     8\timport urllib.error\n     9\timport urllib.request\n    10\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    11\t\n    12\tHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    13\tsys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))\n    14\timport paid_gate as pg                                                  # noqa: E402\n    15\tfrom hivemind import model                                              # noqa: E402\n    16\t\n    17\tPLAN = json.loads((HERE / 'paid-plan.json').read_text())\n    18\tBY_USER = {it['user']: it for it in PLAN}\n    19\tPLAN_MEMBERS = {it['unit']: it['members'] for it in PLAN if it['arm'] in ('joint', 'single')}\n    20\t\n    21\t\n    22\tclass FakeResponse:\n    23\t    def __init__(self, body):\n    24\t        self.body, self.status = body, 200\n    25\t\n    26\t    def read(self):\n    27\t        return self.body\n    28\t\n    29\t    def __enter__(self):\n    30\t        return self\n    31\t\n    32\t    def __exit__(self, *exc):\n    33\t        return False\n    34\t\n    35\t\n    36\tdef mid(band):\n    37\t    lo, hi = band\n    38\t    return (lo + hi) / 2 if lo is not None and hi is not None else (lo + 10 if lo is not None else hi - 10)\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\tdef valid_answer(it, flavour='ok'):\n    42\t    \"\"\"A schema-valid v13 answer that passes every check: one estimate outcome per member, inside its second rung (a part below its\n    43\t    whole), the reference unavailable. Flavours: 'bad-rung' (a rung outside the ladder), 'part-above' (Data Center above the total).\"\"\"\n    44\t    figures, answers = [], []\n    45\t    members = it['members']\n    46\t    for n, view_id in enumerate(members):\n    47\t        m = it['family']['members'][view_id]\n    48\t        band = m['bands'][1]\n    49\t        value = mid(band) - (5.0 * n)                      # the second member (the part) a little lower\n    50\t        if flavour == 'part-above' and n == 1:\n    51\t            value = mid(band) + 30.0\n    52\t        fig = {k: None for k in it['schema']['properties']['figures']['items']['properties']}\n    53\t        fig.update(id=f'o_{view_id}', what=m['what'], basis='forecast', scenario='base', kind='estimate', value=value, unit='USD bn',\n    54\t                   basis_text='rehearsal estimate', rests_on=[])\n    55\t        figures.append(fig)\n    56\t        rung = 2 if not (flavour == 'part-above' and n == 1) else next(i + 1 for i, b in enumerate(m['bands'])\n    57\t                                                                         if (b[0] is None or value >= b[0]) and (b[1] is None or value < b[1]))\n    58\t        ans = {k: None for k in it['schema']['properties']['answers']['items']['properties']}\n    59\t        ans.update(view_id=view_id, shape='forecast', outcome=fig['id'], rung=99 if flavour == 'bad-rung' else rung,\n    60\t                   reference={'figure': None, 'unavailable': 'no market figure in the shown passages'}, reasons='rehearsal', cites=[],\n    61\t                   pushes=[], theme_pushes=[])\n    62\t        answers.append(ans)\n    63\t    return {'figures': figures, 'answers': answers}\n    64\t\n    65\t\n    66\tdef http_error(url, code):\n    67\t    return urllib.error.HTTPError(url, code, f'HTTP {code}', {}, io.BytesIO(json.dumps({'error': {'code': code}}).encode()))\n    68\t\n    69\t\n    70\tclass Stub:\n    71\t    def __init__(self, cfg, scenario, ledger):\n    72\t        self.cfg, self.scenario, self.ledger, self.calls, self.problems, self.sent = cfg, scenario, ledger, {}, [], 0\n    73\t\n    74\t    def expected(self, it, user):\n    75\t        s = self.cfg.rejudging\n    76\t        return json.dumps({'model': s.model, 'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': it['system']}, {'role': 'user', 'content': user}],\n    77\t                           'response_format': {'type': 'json_schema', 'json_schema': {'name': 'judgement', 'strict': True, 'schema': it['schema']}},\n    78\t                           'max_completion_tokens': s.max_output_tokens, 'reasoning_effort': s.reasoning_effort}).encode('utf-8')\n    79\t\n    80\t    def __call__(self, http_request, *args, **kwargs):\n    81\t        body = http_request.data\n    82\t        request = json.loads(body)\n    83\t        user = request['messages'][1]['content']\n    84\t        base = user.split(pg.RETRY_MARK)[0]\n    85\t        it = BY_USER.get(base)\n    86\t        if it is None or body != self.expected(it, user):\n    87\t            self.problems.append('a body that is not the planned request, byte for byte')\n    88\t            raise http_error(http_request.full_url, 400)\n    89\t        key = (it['unit'], it['arm'])\n    90\t        self.calls[key] = self.calls.get(key, 0) + 1\n    91\t        self.sent += 1\n    92\t        n, s = self.calls[key], self.scenario\n    93\t        retry = pg.RETRY_MARK in user\n    94\t        if s == 'ledger-stop' and self.sent == 5:\n    95\t            self.ledger.stop('rehearsal: stopped after four sends')\n    96\t            raise http_error(http_request.full_url, 503)\n    97\t        flavour = 'ok'\n    98\t        if s == 'retry' and key == ('single-O', 'single') and not retry and n == 1:\n    99\t            flavour = 'bad-rung'\n   100\t        if s == 'unresolved' and key == ('single-S', 'single') and n <= 2:\n   101\t            flavour = 'bad-rung'\n   102\t        if s == 'separate-contradiction' and it['arm'].startswith('separate-v9'):\n   103\t            flavour = 'part-above-alone'\n   104\t        data = valid_answer(it, 'ok' if flavour == 'part-above-alone' else flavour)\n   105\t        if flavour == 'part-above-alone':                    # the Data Center card alone, placed above the total's value\n   106\t            data['figures'][0]['value'] = 440.0\n   107\t            data['answers'][0]['rung'] = 2\n   108\t        if s == 'format' and key == ('single-E', 'single') and n == 1:\n   109\t            data['answers'][0].pop('reasons')\n   110\t        usage = {'prompt_tokens': len(body) // 4, 'completion_tokens': 800}\n   111\t        return FakeResponse(json.dumps({'choices': [{'message': {'content': json.dumps(data)}}], 'usage': usage}).encode('utf-8'))\n   112\t\n   113\t\n   114\tdef scenario(scratch, name, ceiling=0.5):\n   115\t    out = scratch / name\n   116\t    out.mkdir(parents=True)\n   117\t    budget = pg.budget_module()\n   118\t    budget.SharedLedger.init(str(out / 'ledger.json'), ceiling)\n   119\t    ledger = budget.SharedLedger(str(out / 'ledger.json'))\n   120\t    gate = pg.Gate(out, budget.BudgetTransport(ledger, sleep=lambda seconds: None), ledger)\n   121\t    (out / 'plan.json').write_text(json.dumps(PLAN))\n   122\t    stub = Stub(gate.cfg, name, ledger)\n   123\t    saved = (urllib.request.urlopen, os.environ.get('OPENAI_API_KEY'))\n   124\t    os.environ['OPENAI_API_KEY'] = 'rehearsal-dummy-not-a-key'\n   125\t    urllib.request.urlopen = stub\n   126\t    remove_gate = budget.install_stop_gate(ledger)\n   127\t    try:\n   128\t        summary = gate.run(PLAN)\n   129\t    finally:\n   130\t        remove_gate()\n   131\t        urllib.request.urlopen = saved[0]\n   132\t        if saved[1] is None:\n   133\t            os.environ.pop('OPENAI_API_KEY', None)\n   134\t        else:\n   135\t            os.environ['OPENAI_API_KEY'] = saved[1]\n   136\t    lines = [json.loads(l) for l in (out / 'answers.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()] if (out / 'answers.jsonl').exists() else []\n   137\t    return summary, lines, stub, ledger.read()\n   138\t\n   139\t\n   140\tdef main(scratch):\n   141\t    scratch = Path(scratch)\n   142\t    checks = []\n   143\t\n   144\t    def check(name, ok, detail=''):\n   145\t        checks.append(ok)\n   146\t        print(f'{\"PASS\" if ok else \"FAIL\"}  {name}  {detail}')\n   147\t\n   148\t    s, lines, stub, led = scenario(scratch, 'clean')\n   149\t    check('clean: 36 first attempts, no retry', len(lines) == 36 and all(l['attempt'] == 1 for l in lines), f'{len(lines)} attempts')\n   150\t    check('clean: every body byte-equal to the planned request', not stub.problems, str(stub.problems[:1]))\n   151\t    check('clean: every unit publishes', all(v['decision'] == 'publish' for v in s['finals'].values()))\n   152\t    check('clean: the separate arm reconciles in all 9 pairs', all(v['decision'] == 'publish' for v in s['reconciled'].values()) and len(s['reconciled']) == 9)\n   153\t    check('clean: spend settled under the ceiling', led['spent'] <= led['ceiling'] and not led.get('stopped'), f'spent {led[\"spent\"]:.4f}')\n   154\t    keydir = scratch / 'key-clean'\n   155\t    pg.packets(scratch / 'clean', keydir)\n   156\t    key = json.loads((keydir / 'packet-key.json').read_text())\n   157\t    check('packets: 27 packets, arms hidden in the text', len(key) == 27 and 'joint' not in (scratch / 'clean' / 'packets.md').read_text()\n   158\t          and 'separate' not in (scratch / 'clean' / 'packets.md').read_text(), f'{len(key)} packets')\n   159\t\n   160\t    def readings(good_separate, defect_in=None, drop=None):\n   161\t        rd = {}\n   162\t        sep_count = {}\n   163\t        for pid, k in key.items():\n   164\t            members = PLAN_MEMBERS[k['unit']]\n   165\t            usable = 'yes'\n   166\t            if k['arm'] == 'separate':\n   167\t                sep_count[k['unit']] = sep_count.get(k['unit'], 0) + 1\n   168\t                usable = 'yes' if sum(sep_count.values()) <= good_separate else 'no'\n   169\t            rd[pid] = {v: {'usable': usable, 'contradiction': 'no', 'internal_reference': 'no', 'deciding_gap': 'no'} for v in members}\n   170\t            if defect_in and k['arm'] == defect_in[0] and defect_in[1] is None:\n   171\t                rd[pid][members[0]]['deciding_gap'] = 'yes'\n   172\t                defect_in = (defect_in[0], 'done')\n   173\t        if drop:\n   174\t            rd.pop(sorted(rd)[0])\n   175\t        return rd\n   176\t\n   177\t    def verdict_of(rd, name):\n   178\t        path = scratch / f'readings-{name}.json'\n   179\t        path.write_text(json.dumps(rd))\n   180\t        return pg.verdict(scratch / 'clean', str(path), keydir)\n   181\t    v = verdict_of(readings(9), 'all-good')\n   182\t    check('verdict: both arms usable everywhere: STOP (gain under 3)', v['verdict'] == 'STOP' and v['joint usable pairs'] == 9 and v['separate usable pairs'] == 9)\n   183\t    v = verdict_of(readings(5), 'gain-4')\n   184\t    check('verdict: joint 9, separate 5: PASS', v['verdict'] == 'PASS', str(v['separate usable pairs']))\n   185\t    v = verdict_of(readings(5, defect_in=('single', None)), 'single-defect')\n   186\t    check('verdict: one published singleton defect: STOP', v['verdict'] == 'STOP' and len(v['published defects']) == 1)\n   187\t    v = verdict_of(readings(5, defect_in=('separate', None)), 'separate-defect')\n   188\t    check('verdict: a defect in the separate arm alone does not stop', v['verdict'] == 'PASS')\n   189\t    v = verdict_of(readings(5, drop=True), 'missing')\n   190\t    check('verdict: a missing reading: INCOMPLETE', v['verdict'] == 'INCOMPLETE')\n   191\t\n   192\t    s, lines, stub, led = scenario(scratch, 'retry')\n   193\t    o = [l for l in lines if l['unit'] == 'single-O' and l['draw'] == 1]\n   194\t    check('retry: a refused calculation is retried once with its errors and then publishes', [l['decision'] for l in o] == ['refused', 'publish'], str([l['decision'] for l in o]))\n   195\t    s, lines, stub, led = scenario(scratch, 'unresolved')\n   196\t    check('unresolved: two refusals make the unit unresolved', s['finals']['single-S|single|1']['decision'] == 'unresolved')\n   197\t    s, lines, stub, led = scenario(scratch, 'format')\n   198\t    e = [l for l in lines if l['unit'] == 'single-E' and l['draw'] == 1]\n   199\t    check('format: a schema-invalid answer is refused, then retried', [l['status'] for l in e] == ['format invalid', 'answered'], str([l['status'] for l in e]))\n   200\t    s, lines, stub, led = scenario(scratch, 'separate-contradiction')\n   201\t    rec = s['reconciled']['pair-old-2|1']\n   202\t    check('separate: two answers that each pass alone are refused when reconciled (C3)', rec['decision'] == 'refused' and any(c == 'C3' for c, _ in rec['errors']),\n   203\t          rec['decision'])\n   204\t    s, lines, stub, led = scenario(scratch, 'ledger-stop')\n   205\t    not_sent = [k for k, v in s['finals'].items() if str(v.get('decision', '')).startswith('not sent')]\n   206\t    check('ledger-stop: after the ledger stops, nothing more is sent', led.get('stopped') and len(lines) == 5 and len(not_sent) >= 30, f'{len(lines)} attempts, {len(not_sent)} not sent')\n   207\t    print(f'{sum(checks)} of {len(checks)} checks pass')\n   208\t    return 0 if all(checks) else 1\n   209\t\n   210\t\n   211\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   212\t    if len(sys.argv) != 2 or sys.argv[1].startswith('-'):\n   213\t        raise SystemExit('usage: paid_rehearsal.py <scratch folder>')\n   214\t    raise SystemExit(main(sys.argv[1]))\nPASS  clean: 36 first attempts, no retry  36 attempts\nPASS  clean: every body byte-equal to the planned request  []\nPASS  clean: every unit publishes  \nPASS  clean: the separate arm reconciles in all 9 pairs  \nPASS  clean: spend settled under the ceiling  spent 0.1156\nPASS  packets: 27 packets, arms hidden in the text  27 packets\nPASS  verdict: both arms usable everywhere: STOP (gain under 3)  \nPASS  verdict: joint 9, separate 5: PASS  5\nPASS  verdict: one published singleton defect: STOP  \nPASS  verdict: a defect in the separate arm alone does not stop  \nPASS  verdict: a missing reading: INCOMPLETE  \nPASS  retry: a refused calculation is retried once with its errors and then publishes  ['refused', 'publish']\nPASS  unresolved: two refusals make the unit unresolved  \nPASS  format: a schema-invalid answer is refused, then retried  ['format invalid', 'answered']\nPASS  separate: two answers that each pass alone are refused when reconciled (C3)  refused\nPASS  ledger-stop: after the ledger stops, nothing more is sent  5 attempts, 31 not sent\n16 of 16 checks pass\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba paid_gate.py | sed -n '1,165p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"The paid gate of judging-v13 (D725's registered test; D729, D730). Harness-only; nothing here is product code.\n     2\t\n     3\t  python3 paid_gate.py plan <out.json>                        # $0: build every request from the stored runs and check them\n     4\t  python3 paid_gate.py send <new out folder> <ceiling>        # paid: only at the ceiling Alex names (APPROVED_CEILING)\n     5\t  python3 paid_gate.py packets <out folder> <key folder>      # $0: blind reading packets, the arm hidden; the key kept outside the repo\n     6\t  python3 paid_gate.py verdict <out folder> <readings.json> <key folder>   # $0: the registered pass and stop lines\n     7\t\n     8\tThe test (D725, RESULT.md): the 09-20 total and Data Center pair in each of three stored draws, judged jointly (one v13 family call)\n     9\tand separately (each member alone, the same union of evidence, the same v13 format), three samples each; plus three samples each of\n    10\tthe O, S and E singletons. 9 + 18 + 9 = 36 first attempts. A calculation the checks refuse is retried once with its errors; a second\n    11\trefusal makes the unit unresolved. The separate arm's two answers are then reconciled by the same checks over the pair's family.\n    12\t\"\"\"\n    13\timport json\n    14\timport random\n    15\timport secrets\n    16\timport sqlite3\n    17\timport sys\n    18\timport threading\n    19\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    20\t\n    21\tHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    22\tREPO = HERE.parents[2]\n    23\tsys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))\n    24\tsys.path.insert(0, str(REPO / 'src'))\n    25\timport calc_check as cc                                                 # noqa: E402\n    26\timport render_v13 as rv                                                 # noqa: E402\n    27\tfrom hivemind import config, model                                      # noqa: E402\n    28\t\n    29\tRUN = REPO / 'poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run'\n    30\tCONFIG = REPO / 'poc/config/poc-v118.json'                              # its re-judging model setting: gpt-6-luna, medium, 16000 output tokens\n    31\tSYSTEM = (HERE / 'judging-v13-draft.txt').read_text()\n    32\tAPPROVED_CEILING = None                                                 # set only from Alex's answer; send refuses while None\n    33\tDRAWS = (1, 2, 3)\n    34\tRETRY_MARK = '\\n\\nThe code refused the previous answer because: '\n    35\tPAIRS = [('old-1', ('v4', 9014), ('v8', 9022)), ('old-2', ('v14', 8729), ('v9', 8737)), ('old-3', ('v3', 9183), ('v35', 9177))]\n    36\tSINGLETONS = [('O', 'old-2', 'v29', 8734, ('NVIDIA', 'equity investment commitments', 'company', 'end of FY2027')),\n    37\t              ('S', 'old-2', 'v6', 8595, ('four largest AI hyperscalers', 'data-center capex', 'combined', 'CY2027')),\n    38\t              ('E', 'old-3', 'v41', 9166, ('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'Vera CPU', 'FY2028'))]\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\tdef W(population, measure, scope, period):\n    42\t    return {'population': population, 'measure': measure, 'scope': scope, 'period': period}\n    43\t\n    44\t\n    45\tdef bands(draw, view_id):\n    46\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{RUN / draw / \"prod/views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    47\t    rows = conn.execute('select lo, hi from rungs where view_id=? order by position', (view_id,)).fetchall()\n    48\t    return [[lo / 1e9 if lo is not None else None, hi / 1e9 if hi is not None else None] for lo, hi in rows]\n    49\t\n    50\t\n    51\tdef passages(draw, evidence_ids):\n    52\t    \"\"\"What each request showed of a passage: the quote cut at 400 characters (judging._lines_english).\"\"\"\n    53\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{RUN / draw / \"prod/views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    54\t    rows = conn.execute(f'select evidence_id, quote, speaker from evidence where evidence_id in ({\",\".join(\"?\" * len(evidence_ids))})',\n    55\t                        evidence_ids).fetchall()\n    56\t    return {e: {'text': (q or '')[:400], 'speaker': s} for e, q, s in rows}\n    57\t\n    58\t\n    59\tdef pair_family(draw, total, dc):\n    60\t    return {'members': {total[0]: {'what': W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027'), 'bands': bands(draw, total[0])},\n    61\t                        dc[0]: {'what': W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'Data Center', 'FY2027'), 'bands': bands(draw, dc[0])}},\n    62\t            'relations': [{'type': 'part_of', 'part': dc[0], 'whole': total[0]}],\n    63\t            'shared': [W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027 Q3'), W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027 Q4')],\n    64\t            'compare_periods': ['FY2027 Q3', 'FY2027 Q4', 'FY2027']}\n    65\t\n    66\t\n    67\tdef only(family, view_id):\n    68\t    return {'members': {view_id: family['members'][view_id]}, 'relations': [], 'shared': family['shared'], 'compare_periods': []}\n    69\t\n    70\t\n    71\tdef item(unit, arm, draw, calls, family, shown):\n    72\t    archive = RUN / draw / 'prod/archive.sqlite'\n    73\t    user, evidence_ids, theme_ids = rv.render(archive, calls, family, shown=shown)\n    74\t    return {'unit': unit, 'arm': arm, 'draw_store': draw, 'members': sorted(shown), 'system': SYSTEM, 'user': user,\n    75\t            'schema': rv.v13_schema(sorted(shown), evidence_ids, theme_ids), 'family': family, 'passages': passages(draw, evidence_ids),\n    76\t            'evidence_ids': evidence_ids}\n    77\t\n    78\t\n    79\tdef build_plan():\n    80\t    items = []\n    81\t    for draw, total, dc in PAIRS:\n    82\t        family = pair_family(draw, total, dc)\n    83\t        calls = [total, dc]\n    84\t        items.append(item(f'pair-{draw}', 'joint', draw, calls, family, [total[0], dc[0]]))\n    85\t        for member in (total, dc):                            # the same union of evidence, one member's header and answer\n    86\t            items.append(item(f'pair-{draw}', f'separate-{member[0]}', draw, calls, only(family, member[0]), [member[0]]))\n    87\t    for name, draw, view_id, call_id, what in SINGLETONS:\n    88\t        family = {'members': {view_id: {'what': W(*what), 'bands': bands(draw, view_id)}}, 'relations': [], 'shared': [], 'compare_periods': []}\n    89\t        items.append(item(f'single-{name}', 'single', draw, [(view_id, call_id)], family, [view_id]))\n    90\t    return items\n    91\t\n    92\t\n    93\tdef plan(out):\n    94\t    items = build_plan()\n    95\t    report = []\n    96\t    for it in items:\n    97\t        missing = sorted(set(it['evidence_ids']) - set(it['passages']))\n    98\t        report.append(f'{it[\"unit\"]:14} {it[\"arm\"]:14} members {it[\"members\"]} user {len(it[\"user\"])} chars, evidence {len(it[\"evidence_ids\"])}, '\n    99\t                      f'schema {len(json.dumps(it[\"schema\"]))} chars, passages missing {missing or \"none\"}')\n   100\t        if missing or 'Outcome keys' not in it['user']:\n   101\t            raise SystemExit(f'{it[\"unit\"]} {it[\"arm\"]}: incomplete request; not planned')\n   102\t    Path(out).write_text(json.dumps(items, indent=1))\n   103\t    print('\\n'.join(report))\n   104\t    print(f'{len(items)} requests x {len(DRAWS)} draws = {len(items) * len(DRAWS)} first attempts')\n   105\t\n   106\t\n   107\tdef strip(data):\n   108\t    return rv.without_nulls(data)\n   109\t\n   110\t\n   111\tclass Gate:\n   112\t    def __init__(self, out, transport, ledger=None):\n   113\t        self.out, self.transport, self.ledger = out, transport, ledger\n   114\t        self.cfg = config.load(str(CONFIG))\n   115\t        self.lock = threading.Lock()\n   116\t        (out / 'archives').mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n   117\t\n   118\t    def request(self, it, user):\n   119\t        return model.build_request(self.cfg.rejudging, it['system'], user, it['schema'], 'judgement', self.cfg.provider)\n   120\t\n   121\t    def record(self, line):\n   122\t        with self.lock, open(self.out / 'answers.jsonl', 'a') as handle:\n   123\t            handle.write(json.dumps(line, ensure_ascii=False) + '\\n')\n   124\t\n   125\t    def attempt(self, it, draw, user, n):\n   126\t        name = f'{it[\"unit\"]}-{it[\"arm\"]}-d{draw}-a{n}.sqlite'\n   127\t        archive = model.Archive(str(self.out / 'archives' / name))\n   128\t        line = {'unit': it['unit'], 'arm': it['arm'], 'draw': draw, 'attempt': n,\n   129\t                'request_sha256': model.request_identity(self.request(it, user))[1]}\n   130\t        try:\n   131\t            answer = model.call(archive, self.cfg, self.cfg.rejudging, it['system'], user, it['schema'], 'judgement', 'judge', transport=self.transport)\n   132\t            calc = strip(answer.data)\n   133\t            result = cc.check(it['family'], it['passages'], calc)\n   134\t            decision = cc.publish_decision(it['family'], calc, result)\n   135\t            line.update(status='answered', data=answer.data, cost_usd=answer.cost_usd, errors=result['errors'], recorded=result['recorded'],\n   136\t                        published=result.get('published'), decision=decision)\n   137\t        except model.SchemaError as error:\n   138\t            line.update(status='format invalid', error=str(error)[:500], decision='refused', errors=[('schema', str(error)[:300])])\n   139\t        except model.TransportError as error:\n   140\t            line.update(status='transport error', error=str(error)[:500], decision='transport')\n   141\t        self.record(line)\n   142\t        return line\n   143\t\n   144\t    def unit(self, it, draw):\n   145\t        first = self.attempt(it, draw, it['user'], 1)\n   146\t        if first['decision'] != 'refused':\n   147\t            return first, [first]\n   148\t        reasons = '; '.join(f'{c}: {d}' for c, d in first.get('errors', []))[:4000]\n   149\t        second = self.attempt(it, draw, it['user'] + RETRY_MARK + reasons, 2)\n   150\t        final = dict(second, decision='unresolved') if second['decision'] == 'refused' else second\n   151\t        return final, [first, second]\n   152\t\n   153\t    def run(self, items):\n   154\t        finals = {}\n   155\t        for draw in DRAWS:\n   156\t            for it in items:\n   157\t                if self.ledger is not None and self.ledger.read().get('stopped'):\n   158\t                    finals[f'{it[\"unit\"]}|{it[\"arm\"]}|{draw}'] = {'decision': 'not sent: the ledger stopped'}\n   159\t                    continue\n   160\t                final, _ = self.unit(it, draw)\n   161\t                finals[f'{it[\"unit\"]}|{it[\"arm\"]}|{draw}'] = {k: final.get(k) for k in ('status', 'decision', 'data', 'errors', 'recorded', 'published')}\n   162\t        reconciled = {}\n   163\t        for draw_store, total, dc in PAIRS:                     # the separate arm, reconciled over the pair's family\n   164\t            for draw in DRAWS:\n   165\t                a, b = (finals.get(f'pair-{draw_store}|separate-{m[0]}|{draw}', {}) for m in (total, dc))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba paid_gate.py | sed -n '166,360p'\"","aggregated_output":"   166\t                if a.get('decision') != 'publish' or b.get('decision') != 'publish':\n   167\t                    reconciled[f'pair-{draw_store}|{draw}'] = {'decision': 'not reconciled', 'members': [a.get('decision'), b.get('decision')]}\n   168\t                    continue\n   169\t                merged = merge([(total[0], strip(a['data'])), (dc[0], strip(b['data']))])\n   170\t                family = pair_family(draw_store, total, dc)\n   171\t                pas = next(i['passages'] for i in items if i['unit'] == f'pair-{draw_store}' and i['arm'] == 'joint')\n   172\t                result = cc.check(family, pas, merged)\n   173\t                reconciled[f'pair-{draw_store}|{draw}'] = {'decision': cc.publish_decision(family, merged, result), 'errors': result['errors'],\n   174\t                                                         'published': result.get('published'), 'calc': merged}\n   175\t        summary = {'finals': finals, 'reconciled': reconciled, 'ledger': self.ledger.read() if self.ledger else None}\n   176\t        (self.out / 'results.json').write_text(json.dumps(summary, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   177\t        return summary\n   178\t\n   179\t\n   180\tdef merge(parts):\n   181\t    \"\"\"Two separate answers as one calculation: each figure id prefixed by its member, so the family's checks see both side by side.\"\"\"\n   182\t    figures, answers = [], []\n   183\t    for view_id, calc in parts:\n   184\t        rename = {f['id']: f'{view_id}.{f[\"id\"]}' for f in calc['figures']}\n   185\t        for f in calc['figures']:\n   186\t            g = dict(f, id=rename[f['id']])\n   187\t            for key in ('inputs', 'rests_on', 'converts'):\n   188\t                if key in g:\n   189\t                    g[key] = [rename.get(x, x) for x in g[key]]\n   190\t            for key in ('disputed', 'bridge'):\n   191\t                if key in g:\n   192\t                    g[key] = rename.get(g[key], g[key])\n   193\t            if 'adjusts' in g:\n   194\t                g['adjusts'] = dict(g['adjusts'], figure=rename.get(g['adjusts']['figure'], g['adjusts']['figure']))\n   195\t            figures.append(g)\n   196\t        for a in calc['answers']:\n   197\t            a2 = dict(a)\n   198\t            if 'outcome' in a2:\n   199\t                a2['outcome'] = rename.get(a2['outcome'], a2['outcome'])\n   200\t            if a2.get('reference', {}).get('figure'):\n   201\t                a2['reference'] = {'figure': rename.get(a2['reference']['figure'], a2['reference']['figure'])}\n   202\t            answers.append(a2)\n   203\t    return {'figures': figures, 'answers': answers}\n   204\t\n   205\t\n   206\tdef budget_module():\n   207\t    import importlib.util\n   208\t    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('budget_replay_v13', REPO / 'clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py')\n   209\t    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n   210\t    spec.loader.exec_module(module)\n   211\t    return module\n   212\t\n   213\t\n   214\tdef send(out, approved, plan_path):\n   215\t    if APPROVED_CEILING is None or approved != APPROVED_CEILING:\n   216\t        raise SystemExit(f'the approved ceiling is {APPROVED_CEILING} (Alex names it); refused')\n   217\t    if out.exists():\n   218\t        raise SystemExit(f'{out} exists: the gate starts from an empty folder')\n   219\t    items = json.loads(Path(plan_path).read_text())\n   220\t    out.mkdir(parents=True)\n   221\t    (out / 'plan.json').write_text(json.dumps(items))\n   222\t    budget = budget_module()\n   223\t    budget.SharedLedger.init(str(out / 'ledger.json'), approved)\n   224\t    ledger = budget.SharedLedger(str(out / 'ledger.json'))\n   225\t    lock_handle = open(out / 'gate.launcher.lock', 'a+')\n   226\t    if not ledger.claim_launcher('v13-gate', lock_handle):\n   227\t        raise SystemExit('another launch is running')\n   228\t    remove_gate = budget.install_stop_gate(ledger)\n   229\t    try:\n   230\t        summary = Gate(out, budget.BudgetTransport(ledger), ledger).run(items)\n   231\t    finally:\n   232\t        remove_gate()\n   233\t        ledger.remove_launcher('v13-gate')\n   234\t    print(json.dumps({k: v.get('decision') for k, v in summary['finals'].items()}, indent=1))\n   235\t\n   236\t\n   237\t# ---------- blind reading ----------\n   238\tQUESTIONS = ('usable: is the card\\'s outcome usable and supported by the shown passages it rests on? (yes/no)',\n   239\t             'contradiction: does the card, with the other card of its packet, state a hard numerical contradiction? (yes/no)',\n   240\t             'internal_reference: is the system\\'s own forecast presented as the market\\'s expectation? (yes/no)',\n   241\t             'deciding_gap: does an unresolved overlap, a change of scope or an unsized adjustment decide the card\\'s band? (yes/no)')\n   242\t\n   243\t\n   244\tdef cards_of(entry):\n   245\t    calc = entry.get('calc') or (strip(entry['data']) if entry.get('data') else None)\n   246\t    return calc\n   247\t\n   248\t\n   249\tdef packets(out, key_dir):\n   250\t    results = json.loads((out / 'results.json').read_text())\n   251\t    items = {(i['unit'], i['arm']): i for i in json.loads((out / 'plan.json').read_text())}\n   252\t    units = []\n   253\t    for key, entry in results['finals'].items():\n   254\t        unit, arm, draw = key.split('|')\n   255\t        if arm.startswith('separate-'):\n   256\t            continue\n   257\t        units.append((unit, arm, draw, entry))\n   258\t    for key, entry in results['reconciled'].items():\n   259\t        unit, draw = key.split('|')\n   260\t        units.append((unit, 'separate', draw, entry))\n   261\t    rng = random.Random(secrets.randbits(64))\n   262\t    rng.shuffle(units)\n   263\t    key, lines = {}, []\n   264\t    for n, (unit, arm, draw, entry) in enumerate(units, 1):\n   265\t        pid = f'P{n:02d}'\n   266\t        key[pid] = {'unit': unit, 'arm': arm, 'draw': draw, 'decision': entry.get('decision')}\n   267\t        it = items[(unit, 'joint' if unit.startswith('pair') else 'single')]\n   268\t        calc = cards_of(entry)\n   269\t        lines.append(f'## {pid}\\nQuestions: {\", \".join(it[\"members\"])}; decision by the code: {entry.get(\"decision\")}')\n   270\t        if calc:\n   271\t            cited = sorted({f['evidence'] for f in calc['figures'] if f.get('evidence')} | {c for a in calc['answers'] for c in a.get('cites', [])})\n   272\t            lines.append('Passages:\\n' + '\\n'.join(f'- {e}: {it[\"passages\"].get(e, {}).get(\"text\", \"(not shown)\")}' for e in cited))\n   273\t            lines.append('Figures:\\n' + '\\n'.join(f'- {json.dumps(f, ensure_ascii=False)}' for f in calc['figures']))\n   274\t            lines.append('Cards:\\n' + '\\n'.join(f'- {json.dumps(a, ensure_ascii=False)}' for a in calc['answers']))\n   275\t        lines.append('Answer for each card: ' + ' | '.join(QUESTIONS) + '\\n')\n   276\t    key_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n   277\t    (key_dir / 'packet-key.json').write_text(json.dumps(key, indent=1))\n   278\t    (out / 'packets.md').write_text('\\n'.join(lines))\n   279\t    print(f'{len(units)} packets; key in {key_dir}')\n   280\t\n   281\t\n   282\tdef verdict(out, readings_path, key_dir):\n   283\t    \"\"\"D725's registered lines. readings: {packet id: {view id: {usable, contradiction, internal_reference, deciding_gap}}}.\"\"\"\n   284\t    key = json.loads((key_dir / 'packet-key.json').read_text())\n   285\t    readings = json.loads(Path(readings_path).read_text())\n   286\t    usable_pairs = {'joint': {}, 'separate': {}}\n   287\t    defects = []\n   288\t    for pid, k in key.items():\n   289\t        cards = readings.get(pid, {})\n   290\t        if k['decision'] == 'publish' and k['arm'] in ('joint', 'single'):      # D725: defects count across the joint and singleton answers\n   291\t            for view_id, r in cards.items():\n   292\t                if r.get('contradiction') == 'yes' or r.get('internal_reference') == 'yes' or r.get('deciding_gap') == 'yes':\n   293\t                    defects.append((pid, k['unit'], k['arm'], view_id))\n   294\t        if k['unit'].startswith('pair') and k['arm'] in usable_pairs:\n   295\t            ok = k['decision'] == 'publish' and len(cards) == 2 and all(r.get('usable') == 'yes' for r in cards.values())\n   296\t            usable_pairs[k['arm']].setdefault(k['unit'], []).append(ok)\n   297\t    joint_total = sum(sum(v) for v in usable_pairs['joint'].values())\n   298\t    separate_total = sum(sum(v) for v in usable_pairs['separate'].values())\n   299\t    per_snapshot = {u: sum(v) for u, v in usable_pairs['joint'].items()}\n   300\t    readable = all(pid in readings and len(readings[pid]) == (2 if k['unit'].startswith('pair') else 1) for pid, k in key.items())\n   301\t    complete = (len(key) == 27 and readable and len(usable_pairs['joint']) == 3 and len(usable_pairs['separate']) == 3\n   302\t                and all(len(v) == 3 for arm in usable_pairs.values() for v in arm.values()))\n   303\t    passes = complete and not defects and joint_total >= 8 and all(n >= 2 for n in per_snapshot.values()) and joint_total - separate_total >= 3\n   304\t    summary = {'complete': complete, 'joint usable pairs': joint_total, 'separate usable pairs': separate_total, 'joint per snapshot': per_snapshot,\n   305\t               'published defects': defects, 'verdict': 'PASS' if passes else ('INCOMPLETE' if not complete else 'STOP')}\n   306\t    print(json.dumps(summary, indent=1))\n   307\t    return summary\n   308\t\n   309\t\n   310\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   311\t    cmd = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else ''\n   312\t    if cmd == 'plan' and len(sys.argv) == 3:\n   313\t        plan(sys.argv[2])\n   314\t    elif cmd == 'send' and len(sys.argv) == 5 and not sys.argv[2].startswith('-'):\n   315\t        send(Path(sys.argv[2]), float(sys.argv[3]), sys.argv[4])\n   316\t    elif cmd == 'packets' and len(sys.argv) == 4:\n   317\t        packets(Path(sys.argv[2]), Path(sys.argv[3]))\n   318\t    elif cmd == 'verdict' and len(sys.argv) == 5:\n   319\t        verdict(Path(sys.argv[2]), sys.argv[3], Path(sys.argv[4]))\n   320\t    else:\n   321\t        raise SystemExit(__doc__)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba PAID-GATE.md; nl -ba RESULT.md; rg -n '\"'^## D(725|728|729|730)'\"' ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba PAID-GATE.md; nl -ba RESULT.md; rg -n '\"'^## D(725|728|729|730)'\"' ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# judging-v13 paid gate: plan, harness and reading rule (registered before any send; D725, D729, D730)\n     2\t\n     3\t## 1. What is sent\n     4\t\n     5\t`paid_gate.py plan paid-plan.json` builds 12 requests from the stored runs.\n     6\t\n     7\t| Unit | Arm | Members | Evidence shown |\n     8\t|---|---|---|---|\n     9\t| pair-old-1 (09-20: v4 total, v8 Data Center) | joint; separate-v4; separate-v8 | both; one; one | the union of both stored requests' evidence in view (237 items), in every arm |\n    10\t| pair-old-2 (v14, v9) | joint; separate-v14; separate-v9 | as above | 237 |\n    11\t| pair-old-3 (v3, v35) | joint; separate-v3; separate-v35 | as above | 260 |\n    12\t| single-O (old-2 v29, equity commitments) | single | v29 | its own request's (35) |\n    13\t| single-S (old-2 v6, four hyperscalers' 2027 capex) | single | v6 | 31 |\n    14\t| single-E (old-3 v41, FY2028 Vera CPU) | single | v41 | 15 |\n    15\t\n    16\t- **Each request:** judging-v13's system text (`judging-v13-draft.txt`, 4,373 characters); the family header with the exact outcome\n    17\t  keys; the evidence; the themes once. No earlier forecast is shown (D728). The strict v13 schema.\n    18\t- **The model:** poc-v118's re-judging setting (gpt-6-luna, medium effort, 16,000 output tokens).\n    19\t- **Draws:** three per request, so 36 first attempts.\n    20\t- **Retry:** a calculation the checks refuse, or a schema-invalid answer, is retried once with the reasons. A second refusal makes the\n    21\t  unit unresolved.\n    22\t- **The separate arm:** its two answers per pair and draw are merged and checked over the pair's family (C3, C4 across the two).\n    23\t\n    24\t## 2. Spend and stops\n    25\t\n    26\t- **The ledger:** one, at Alex's ceiling (`paid_gate.py send <folder> <ceiling> paid-plan.json` refuses any other ceiling).\n    27\t- **Budget:** the real budget transport and stop gate, which reserve each request's worst case before sending. After a stop, nothing\n    28\t  more is sent, and the remaining units are recorded as not sent.\n    29\t- **Estimate:** about $0.004–0.008 a call, so $0.15–0.30 for 36, plus retries. **Proposed ceiling: $0.50.**\n    30\t- **Sends:** one at a time. Each send has its own archive, so no draw is answered from another.\n    31\t\n    32\t## 3. The $0 rehearsal (`paid_rehearsal.py`, `rehearsal.log`: 16 of 16)\n    33\t\n    34\t- **Clean run:** 36 first attempts, every HTTP body byte-equal to an independently built request, every unit published, the separate\n    35\t  arm reconciled in 9 of 9, the spend settled under the ceiling.\n    36\t- **Paths:**\n    37\t  - a refused calculation is retried, then published;\n    38\t  - two refusals give unresolved;\n    39\t  - a schema-invalid answer is retried;\n    40\t  - two separate answers that each pass alone are refused when reconciled (C3);\n    41\t  - after a ledger stop, nothing more is sent.\n    42\t- **Packets:** 27 packets with the arm hidden. The verdict is computed on synthetic readings: both arms good gives STOP (gain under 3);\n    43\t  a joint gain of 4 gives PASS; one published singleton defect gives STOP; a separate-arm defect alone does not stop; a missing\n    44\t  reading gives INCOMPLETE.\n    45\t\n    46\t## 4. The reading rule (fixed now, before any answer exists)\n    47\t\n    48\t- **Packets:** 27 (`paid_gate.py packets`): 9 joint pair-draws, 9 reconciled separate pair-draws and 9 singleton draws. The labels are\n    49\t  shuffled, the arm is hidden, and the key is kept in `~/.hivemind-keys/v13-paid-gate/`.\n    50\t  - Each packet shows the questions, every passage a figure or citation names (as the request showed it), the figures and the cards.\n    51\t  - A packet the code did not publish (held, unresolved, not reconciled) is read too. Its cards cannot count as usable.\n    52\t- **Readers:** two fresh readers of different families, a Codex session and a Claude subagent, each blind to the other and to the arm.\n    53\t  For each card each answers four questions, yes or no, with the passage that decides:\n    54\t  1. **usable:** the outcome is usable and supported by the shown passages it rests on;\n    55\t  2. **contradiction:** with the other card of its packet, it states a hard numerical contradiction;\n    56\t  3. **internal_reference:** the system's own forecast is presented as the market's expectation;\n    57\t  4. **deciding_gap:** an unresolved overlap, a change of scope or an unsized adjustment decides its band.\n    58\t- **Agreement:** where the two readers agree, that is the reading. Where they disagree, a third fresh reader (Codex) reads the card with\n    59\t  both readings and the passages, and its answer decides. No reading is changed after the verdict is computed.\n    60\t- **Verdict** (`paid_gate.py verdict`, D725's lines):\n    61\t  - **PASS:** the joint arm has both cards usable in at least 8 of 9 pairs, at least 2 of 3 per snapshot, and at least 3 more usable\n    62\t    pairs than the separate arm; and zero published defects (contradiction, internal reference or deciding gap) across the joint and\n    63\t    singleton answers.\n    64\t  - **STOP:** any such published defect; a coverage line missed; a gain under 3.\n    65\t  - **INCOMPLETE:** a packet or a card missing a reading, or a unit not sent.\n    66\t  - This is a small design test, not release acceptance.\n    67\t\n    68\t## 5. What the result decides\n    69\t\n    70\t- **PASS:** judging-v13 earns a production design: automatic families in matching, lifecycle and the request builder, each a further\n    71\t  step Alex opens.\n    72\t- **STOP or INCOMPLETE:** the line goes back to Alex with the readings, and nothing is tuned on these 36 answers.\n     1\t# Why the number answers cannot be trusted: council round 45/45b (2026-11-22, consensus, $0)\n     2\t\n     3\tAlex asked to step back and find which part of the design produces the unreliable numbers. The record:\n     4\t- `round45-brief.md`;\n     5\t- `claude-r45.md` (written before Codex);\n     6\t- `codex-r45.md` (an independent investigation, fresh thread `01a20501…`, read-only, no model calls);\n     7\t- `round45b-brief.md` and `codex-r45b.md` (the challenge round).\n     8\t\n     9\t## The answer\n    10\t\n    11\tThe system has no single, checked calculation behind its related numbers:\n    12\t- **Each number question is judged alone.** It rebuilds the company's numbers from its own slice of evidence, with its own bases and\n    13\t  its own reference.\n    14\t- **It publishes the result as prose.** Code cannot tell a sourced figure from an assumption, and never recomputes anything.\n    15\t\n    16\tContradictions between related questions and unsupported figures are what this design produces. They are not one prompt sentence's\n    17\tfault.\n    18\t\n    19\t## What the traces show (three finished poc-v118 draws, 07-01..09-20)\n    20\t\n    21\t- **Cross-question contradictions:**\n    22\t  - old-2 at 09-20: Data Center Q4 is about $146B, the whole company's Q4 about $127B. In old-1 on 09-20 it is $126B against $112.2B.\n    23\t  - A stated segment Q4 above the company Q4 on at least 13 of 26 paired post-earnings days in old-1, and at least 1 in old-2.\n    24\t  - Data Center's full year above total revenue's full year on 20 consecutive days in old-2 (08-26..09-14). Claude checked 08-28, 09-05\n    25\t    and 09-12: $419B, $422B and $414B against $407B.\n    26\t- **Different bases for the same quarter:** on 17 of 18 paired days, 09-15..09-20, Data Center used the $108B Q3 guide while total\n    27\t  revenue used a beat-adjusted Q3 of about $113.5B.\n    28\t- **Disjoint inputs:** old-2's two questions share 106 of about 1,300 linked evidence items. Their 09-20 requests share 5 entries and\n    29\t  cite none in common. Across draws, total against CPU shares 0–5%. The SemiAnalysis uplift was filed under Data Center only.\n    30\t- **Unsupported arithmetic:** in 17 of the 24 answers both readers rejected, the figures came from:\n    31\t  - adding amounts of unknown overlap (#36: $25B + $18B);\n    32\t  - another scope's figure scaled by a mismatched ratio (#38: 730/800 × $1.3T);\n    33\t  - a stacked uplift (#44);\n    34\t  - an unsized trim (#48);\n    35\t  - the system's own earlier figure presented as the market's (old-2 v9: $414B; 44 of 2,375 flagged).\n    36\t- **The production check passes them:** six saved answers still pass with a contradictory forecast or an invented reference\n    37\t  substituted. Only a citation outside the request fails (`judging.check_answer`: rung range, ids, pushes, non-empty fields).\n    38\t\n    39\t## The design causes, ranked\n    40\t\n    41\t1. **Answers are prose with one answer-wide citation list.** No figure is tied to its source, and nothing recomputes. This explains\n    42\t   most of the 24.\n    43\t2. **Related questions compute shared quantities separately.** The judging unit is one question, with 0 dependencies in 139\n    44\t   questions. This explains the contradictions.\n    45\t3. **Filing (narrowest question) and the evidence in view (D198) give related questions different inputs.** The previous conclusion\n    46\t   carries figures without provenance, which is the self-made reference.\n    47\t4. **Opening's bands and pull mode amplify a bad figure:** where the boundary sits decides when the error shows.\n    48\t\n    49\tLinking passed one question's conclusion to another, but not its assumptions. Data Center stopped exceeding the total in the pilot, but\n    50\tthe total added a CPU forecast whose overlap was unresolved (D721).\n    51\t\n    52\t## The converged design (for a new judge version Alex opens)\n    53\t\n    54\t- **One judging call per related family.** Same company and fiscal year, overlapping quantities. Each question keeps its own answer,\n    55\t  and every answer reads from one calculation.\n    56\t- **The judge labels the figures it uses:** what each measures (population, scope, period) and whether it is a source figure, a\n    57\t  calculation or an assumption. Extraction v74i is unchanged.\n    58\t- **Code checks identity and arithmetic only:**\n    59\t  1. a source figure appears in the shown passage it cites;\n    60\t  2. the arithmetic recomputes;\n    61\t  3. a declared part fits within its whole for the same period and scenario;\n    62\t  4. one value per shared quantity, role and scenario across the family;\n    63\t  5. a market reference points to shown external material, or says none.\n    64\t\n    65\t  The model keeps importance: drivers, weights, discounts, and overlap stated as an assumption. A blind reader judges whether an\n    66\t  assumption that crosses a boundary is supported.\n    67\t- **When figures cannot be reconciled, the forecast shows as unresolved,** not as two incompatible answers.\n    68\t- **Bounded to the figures the open questions consume** (D24, D28).\n    69\t- **Families:** declared from stored cases for the test. Production would need a matching version that names the relationship.\n    70\t- **The frozen gold's reasoning is kept:** q01 (upside drivers without a fixed increment), q02 (a segment from the shared total and a\n    71\t  sourced mix), q19 (an execution discount), q22 (FY2028 from q01's base, widened by judgement).\n    72\t\n    73\t## The interim for a first release\n    74\t\n    75\tPublish questions, evidence and events, and show number questions as \"Forecast unavailable\": the band, the forecast text and its\n    76\thistory withheld together (`bundle.py`).\n    77\t\n    78\t## The one test (registered with the design)\n    79\t\n    80\t- **The $0 gate.** Hand-reconstruct, in the new format:\n    81\t  - old-2 8729/8737, 8734 and 8595, and old-3 9166;\n    82\t  - the four gold controls;\n    83\t  - three planted errors (an amount absent from its quote, a wrong sum, an internal forecast labelled consensus).\n    84\t\n    85\t  The format must expose every defect, represent every control, and fail every plant. Any miss stops the line.\n    86\t- **The paid gate** (Alex's ceiling; 36 calls, about $0.2–0.4 estimated):\n    87\t  - **The arms:** the 09-20 total and Data Center pair in each draw, three samples each, judged jointly and separately under the same\n    88\t    format and checks. Plus three samples each on the O, S and E requests. Every output is read against its source with the arm\n    89\t    hidden.\n    90\t  - **Pass:** the joint arm publishes both answers usable and source-supported in at least 8 of 9 pairs, at least 2 of 3 per snapshot,\n    91\t    and at least 3 more usable pairs than the separate arm. Zero published hard contradictions, internal-as-market references, or\n    92\t    unresolved overlap, scope or unsized adjustments that decide the band.\n    93\t  - **Stop:** any such published defect, either coverage line missed, or an incomplete comparison.\n10957:## D725 · 2026-11-22 · Council round 45/45b: the number answers fail because related numbers have no shared, checked calculation; one judge version and one test recommended to Alex\n11041:## D728 · 2026-11-22 · Alex: the family judge does not see its earlier forecasts while calculating\n11055:## D729 · 2026-11-22 · judging-v13's $0 gate passes (council round 46ad); the paid gate needs its harness built at $0 and Alex's ceiling\n11073:## D730 · 2026-11-22 · Alex: build the paid gate's harness at $0, then ask for the ceiling\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
