hed defects': [], 'verdict': 'PASS'}\nschema-valid arithmetic failure: ZeroDivisionError float division by zero rows recorded: 0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c '\nimport sqlite3,json,paid_gate as g\nfor draw,*pairs in g.PAIRS:\n    db=sqlite3.connect(f'\\\\''file:{g.RUN / draw / \\\"prod/views.sqlite\\\"}?mode=ro'\\\\'',uri=True)\n    for v,i in pairs:\n        print(draw,i,db.execute('\\\\''select j.view_id,j.publication_day,v.question from judgements j join views v on v.view_id=j.view_id where call_id=?'\\\\'',(i,)).fetchone())\nfor label,draw,v,i,what in g.SINGLETONS:\n    db=sqlite3.connect(f'\\\\''file:{g.RUN / draw / \\\"prod/views.sqlite\\\"}?mode=ro'\\\\'',uri=True)\n    print(label,draw,i,db.execute('\\\\''select j.view_id,j.publication_day,v.question from judgements j join views v on v.view_id=j.view_id where call_id=?'\\\\'',(i,)).fetchone())\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c '\nimport sqlite3,json,paid_gate as g\nfor draw,*pairs in g.PAIRS:\n    db=sqlite3.connect(f'\\\\''file:{g.RUN / draw / \\\"prod/views.sqlite\\\"}?mode=ro'\\\\'',uri=True)\n    for v,i in pairs:\n        print(draw,i,db.execute('\\\\''select j.view_id,j.publication_day,v.question from judgements j join views v on v.view_id=j.view_id where call_id=?'\\\\'',(i,)).fetchone())\nfor label,draw,v,i,what in g.SINGLETONS:\n    db=sqlite3.connect(f'\\\\''file:{g.RUN / draw / \\\"prod/views.sqlite\\\"}?mode=ro'\\\\'',uri=True)\n    print(label,draw,i,db.execute('\\\\''select j.view_id,j.publication_day,v.question from judgements j join views v on v.view_id=j.view_id where call_id=?'\\\\'',(i,)).fetchone())\n'\"","aggregated_output":"old-1 9014 ('v4', '2026-09-20', \"What will NVIDIA's total revenue be in FY2027?\")\nold-1 9022 ('v8', '2026-09-20', 'How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?')\nold-2 8729 ('v14', '2026-09-20', 'How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?')\nold-2 8737 ('v9', '2026-09-20', 'How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?')\nold-3 9183 ('v3', '2026-09-20', 'What will NVIDIA report as total revenue for FY2027?')\nold-3 9177 ('v35', '2026-09-20', 'What will NVIDIA report as data-center revenue for FY2027?')\nO old-2 8734 ('v29', '2026-09-20', \"How much will NVIDIA's equity investment commitments reach at the publication of its FY2027 annual report?\")\nS old-2 8595 ('v6', '2026-09-19', 'How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?')\nE old-3 9166 ('v41', '2026-09-20', 'What will NVIDIA report as Vera CPU revenue for FY2028?')\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"agent_message","text":"NOT READY\n\nThe saved plan matches D725’s three September 20 pairs and O/S/E singletons, with 36 first attempts. I verified that all three arms for each pair receive identical evidence and themes, the outcome keys match the questions, and no earlier forecast is shown. The harness does not exercise D728’s post-publication change detection. Five issues block the send. [Saved plan](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid-plan.json) · [Registered test](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RESULT.md:78)\n\n1. **Reconciliation penalizes the separate arm even when its numbers agree.** I split the passing R1c calculation into two answers. Both passed alone, but their merge failed C4 because prefixing IDs created two copies each of the *same* Q3 and Q4 forecasts. Before rechecking, reconcile matching quantity, role and scenario forecasts with equal recomputed values and bounds. Preserve conflicts and both derivations. Rehearse one agreeing pair and one disagreeing pair that both contain shared quarters. [Merge](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:162)\n\n2. **The ceiling applies per folder, and the reviewed plan is unpinned.** Each new folder gets a fresh ledger at the approved amount. Two launches can therefore each spend against the full ceiling. The saved plan gives every sample its own archive, but the sender accepts arbitrary plan JSON, and duplicate entries can reuse an archive. Bind one authorization, ledger and launch lock to the reviewed plan and configuration. Validate unique sample IDs before sending. [Archives](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:125) · [Sender](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:214)\n\n3. **A paid answer can leave no attempt record.** A schema-valid answer containing division by zero raised out of `attempt()` with zero rows recorded. Persist the attempt before dispatch, log the raw response and checker failure, and give every planned unit a final status even after an abort. Rehearse this alongside a reservation refusal before the provider is called. [Attempt handling](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:125)\n\n4. **The verdict can pass an incomplete comparison.** My replay returned `PASS` with all three defect fields omitted and an unsent singleton represented by an invented card ID. The coverage and gain thresholds match the registered test, but the code checks reading counts without validating identities, fields or send status. Validate the exact units and cards against the run, require all four readings and their source grounds, and retain both independent readings and any adjudication before computing the verdict. [Verdict](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:282)\n\n5. **The packets omit material the readers need and expose the arm.** They show view IDs in place of question text and bands, omit canonical amounts and assumption records, and miss passages named only in `rests_on`. They also drop first attempts and available separate cards when reconciliation cannot run. Separate-arm ID prefixes and `not reconciled` reveal the arm. Generate one fixed set of packets with the actual questions, bands, dated and attributed evidence, raw and recomputed amounts, and every attempt or explicit failure record. Normalize IDs and status labels before blinding. [Packet builder](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:237)"}}
